hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","2398 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it into it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure."
"2402","2399 - And with the same chain the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dumb animal is an absolved injury, the well is an absolved injury, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"2403","2400 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ayyub and Habib and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied up to withhold its milk has the option for three days; if he wishes he may return it along with a sa of food, not samra."
"2404","2401 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Shabur, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: a man who came upon a people firmly upon Islam and split their unity until they deemed forbidden things lawful and shed blood; and an unjust ruler. And he said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Sufyan remained silent about the third and did not mention it."
"2405","2402 - And with the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while possessing forty dirhams or their value is importunate, and it is like sipping water."
"2406","2403 - And with the same chain from Dawud ibn Shabur, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel continued to enjoin upon me the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."
"2407","2404 - And with the same chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the Quran from four: two men from the Muhajirin and two men from the Ansar: from Abd Allah ibn Masud, Salim freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy ibn Kab, and Muadh ibn Jabal. He singled out Abd Allah ibn Masud with a statement, saying: Whoever wishes to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite with the recitation of Ibn Masud. No one narrated these hadiths from Dawud ibn Shabur except Sufyan; al-Ramadi is alone in transmitting them."
"2408","2405 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Waqii narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, that he said to him: O Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, beware of hating us, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one hates us or envies us except that he will be driven away from the Basin on the Day of Resurrection with whips of fire. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Abd Allah."
"2409","2406 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like a fortified fortress and protection? - meaning a fortress belonging to Daws in pre-Islamic times - but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused that because of what Allah had stored for the Ansar. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) emigrated to Madinah, al-Tufayl ibn Amr emigrated to him, and a man of his people emigrated with him. The man found Madinah unhealthy, so he despaired, took arrowheads of his, cut his knuckles with them, and his hands bled profusely until he died. Al-Tufayl ibn Amr saw him in a dream in a good state, covering his hands. He said: What did your Lord do with you? He said: He forgave me because of my emigration to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Why do I see you covering your hands? He said: It was said to me: We shall never repair what you ruined. Al-Tufayl related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger said: O Allah, forgive his hands too. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Hajjaj; Hammad is alone in transmitting it."
"2410","2407 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abd Allah ibn Ukaym who said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in the land of Juhaynah two months before his death: Do not benefit from carrion by hide or sinew. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Shaybah except Abu Umar."
"2411","2408 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, he said: al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that a sheep belonging to Maymunah died, so we tanned its skin and would make nabidh in it until it became a worn-out waterskin. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Hushaym."
"2412","2409 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate against four men, then Allah Almighty revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers. So Allah guided them to Islam."
"2413","2410 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Zayd al-Taghlibi informed us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the Fire will be made enormous for the Fire, until what lies between the earlobe and the shoulder becomes a journey of seven hundred years, the thickness of his skin forty cubits, and his molar greater than Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya except Imran."
"2414","2411 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that Allah magnify his provision and extend his lifespan, let him join his kinship. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Husayn except Muslim."
"2415","2412 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: al-Yaman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink in three breaths. No one narrated this hadith from Yaman except Hajjaj."
"2416","2413 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Habib ibn Abi Amrah, from Yala ibn Siyabah, that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and passed by a grave whose occupant was being punished, and said: This one used to eat the flesh of people. Then he called for a moist palm frond, placed it upon his grave, and said: Perhaps it will lighten for him as long as it remains moist. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Hammad."
"2417","2414 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah who said: Abd Allah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of need: Praise be to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides none can misguide, and whomever He misguides none can guide. I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O you who believe, fear Allah and speak upright words - the verse; O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims; O mankind, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Abu Umar."
"2418","2415 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ararah narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I accompanied Jarir and he would serve me, though he was older than Anas. Jarir said: I saw the Ansar doing something with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) such that I love everyone among them for it. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Muhammad."
"2419","2416 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hakam narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd narrating from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The king of Rome gifted gifts to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among what he gifted him was a jar containing ginger; he fed each person a piece and fed me a piece. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Amr."
"2420","2417 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from his grandfather Anas, that a Jewish woman brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a poisoned sheep, and he ate from it. She was brought, and it was said: Shall we not kill her? He said: No. I continued to recognize it in the uvulas of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Khalid and Rawh ibn Ubadah."
"2421","2418 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me that Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed him that his father al-Aswad said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taking people's pledge at Qarn Masfalah; men and women, young and old came to him and pledged to him upon Islam and the testimony. I said: What is the testimony? Muhammad ibn al-Aswad informed me, saying: Upon testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from al-Aswad except with this chain; Ibn Jurayj is alone in transmitting it."
"2422","2419 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the rows, for if there is any deficiency it is in the last row. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Abu Asim."
"2423","2420 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah and Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only forbade pure silk; if its warp or weft is silk, there is no harm in wearing it. And he forbade the silver vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf, from Said and Ikrimah except Ibn Jurayj."
"2424","2421 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Abd Allah ibn Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Qurt who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of days with Allah is the Day of Sacrifice, then the Day of Qarr, in which people settle, which follows the Day of Sacrifice. Five or six camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they began crowding toward him, with which of them he would begin. When their sides fell, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said a hidden word I did not understand, so I said to the one beside me: What did he say? He said: Whoever wishes may cut off. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Qurt except with this chain; Thawr is alone in transmitting it."
"2425","2422 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Wahb Abu Khalid who said: Umm Habibah bint al-Irbad ibn Sariyah narrated to me, from her father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every fanged beast of prey and every taloned bird, and forbade the tied-up living target, and that pregnant women be approached until they deliver what is in their wombs."
"2426","2423 - And with the same chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a tuft of wool from the spoils and said: I have of this only what one of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return the thread and the needle, and beware of misappropriation, for it is disgrace, shame, and fire. These two hadiths are not narrated from al-Irbad except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting them."
"2427","2424 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Yahya informed us, he said: My uncle Umarah ibn Thawban informed me that Abu al-Tufayl informed him, saying: I was a boy carrying a camel's limb, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributing meat at al-Ji'ranah. A woman came to him and he spread his cloak for her. I said: Who is she? It was said: His mother who nursed him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Tufayl except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"2428","2425 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Yahya informed us, from his uncle Umarah ibn Thawban, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst are the last of them; the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst are the first of them. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"2429","2426 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn al-Harith who said: Abu Mishrah - or Mishras - narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Shaybah al-Khudri saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Shaybah except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"2430","2427 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn al-Harith who said: Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to us, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer upon the back of a mount is like this and like this and like this."
"2431","2428 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Wabr ibn Abi Dulaylah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Maymun, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The delay of the solvent debtor makes lawful his honor and his punishment. This hadith is not narrated from al-Sharid except with this chain; Wabr is alone in transmitting it. Sufyan narrated it from Wabr and Sufyan explained it, saying: His honor is that he complains against him, and his punishment is his imprisonment."
"2432","2429 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to recite poetry, saying: Do you narrate anything of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt? So I recited to him one hundred rhymes, and each time I passed a verse he said: Go on. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He nearly accepted Islam in his poetry."
"2433","2430 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Rabiah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hisn al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Sarra bint Nabhan narrated to me - and she was a housewife in pre-Islamic times - who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Do you know what day this is? She said: It is the day they call the Day of Heads. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the middle of the days of Tashriq. He said: Do you know what land this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the Sacred Monument. Then he said: I may not meet you after this year of mine. Indeed your blood, wealth, and honors are sacred upon you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, until you meet your Lord and He questions you about your deeds. Let the nearest among you convey to the farthest. Have I conveyed? When we arrived in Madinah we remained only a little until he died, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Sarra bint Nabhan except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"2434","2431 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Farisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih al-Khuzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not ask Him, Almighty, He becomes angry with him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salih except Abu al-Malih."
"2435","2432 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abu al-Jarrah who said: Jabir ibn Salih narrated to me, from Umm Sharahil, from Umm Atiyyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali in a detachment, and I saw him raising his hands, saying: O Allah, do not cause me to die until You show me Ali. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Atiyyah except with this chain; Abu Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"2436","2433 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Jundub ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection, so beware lest Allah overpower you regarding anything of His protection."
"2437","2434 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except al-Ansari."
"2438","2435 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fada narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade breaking the lawful coinage of Muslims current among them except for a defect: that a dirham be broken to be made silver, or a dinar be broken to be made gold. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah al-Muzani except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Fada is alone in transmitting it."
"2439","2436 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combing except every other day."
"2440","2437 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, that Umar went out to pray for rain, taking al-Abbas with him to pray for rain, saying: O Allah, when we suffered drought in the time of our Prophet we would seek mediation to You through our Prophet; O Allah, we now seek mediation to You through the uncle of our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"2441","2438 - And with the same chain from Thumamah, from Anas who said: The engraving of the seal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was three lines: one line: Muhammad, one line: Messenger, and one line: Allah."
"2442","2439 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Numan ibn Bashir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there will be tribulations like pieces of the dark night; a man will wake a believer and sleep a disbeliever; therein peoples will sell their share for a small price of this world. This hadith is not narrated from al-Numan except with this chain; Mubarak is alone in transmitting it."
"2443","2440 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters upon his brother and he feeds him of his food, let him eat and not ask about it; and if he gives him of his drink to drink, let him drink and not ask about it. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd except Muslim."
"2444","2441 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Said ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Hubshi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts a lote tree, Allah will plunge his head into the Fire - meaning of the lote of the Sanctuary. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Habashi except with this chain; Ibn Jurayj is alone in transmitting it."
"2445","2442 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Ururah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, regarding the building of the Ka'bah, who said: When they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enter through the door, they said: The Trustworthy has come. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Hammad."
"2446","2443 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Yasar, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not enter Paradise, and three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection. As for the three who will not enter Paradise: the disobedient to his parents, the dayyuth, and the masculine woman imitating men. As for the three whom Allah will not look at: the disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds of what he gave. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-A'raj; Umar ibn Muhammad al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"2447","2444 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Abu Taybah cupped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Uyaynah ibn Hisn or al-Aqra ibn Habis entered upon him and said: What is this? He said: This is cupping, and it is the best you treat yourselves with."
"2448","2445 - And with the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram due to pain he felt in his head. No one narrated these two hadiths from Humayd except Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Umari."
"2449","2446 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhabbab Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi who said: We would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when anything of the Quran descended upon him he would tell us. One day he said to us: Allah Almighty said: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakah; and if the son of Adam had a valley of wealth he would seek a second to it, and if he had the second he would seek a third to it. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"2450","2447 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham the muezzin narrated to us, from Awf, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he awoke in Makkah, sat apart grieving, and the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl passed by him, saying mockingly: Was there anything? He said: Yes. He said: What? He said: I was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: Then you awoke among us? He said: Yes. He did not show him that he disbelieved him, fearing that if he called his people to him he would deny the account. He said: What if I call your people to you, will you relate to them what you related to me? He said: Yes. So Abu Jahl said: Relate to your people what you related to me. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was taken by night. They said: To where? He said: To Bayt al-Maqdis. They said: Then you awoke among us? He said: Yes. Some clapped and some placed their hands upon their heads in amazement at the lie, as he claimed; and among the people were those who had traveled to that mosque. They said: Can you describe the mosque to us? He said: Yes. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I described it to them until part of the description became confused for me; then the mosque was brought while I looked at it until it was placed before the house of Aqil - or the house of Iqal - and I began describing it to them while looking at it. The people said: As for the description, by Allah he is right. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Abbas except with this chain; Awf is alone in transmitting it."
"2451","2448 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may act with the deeds of the people of Paradise for seventy years, then his end is sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire, so he becomes of the people of the Fire; and a servant may act with the deeds of the people of the Fire for seventy years, then his end is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise, so he becomes of the people of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Khubayb except Abd Allah."
"2452","2449 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Shayban Abu Muawiyah informed us, from Mansur, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Urfutah al-Sulami, from Khidash Abu Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I enjoin a man regarding his mother, I enjoin a man regarding his father, I enjoin a man regarding his freedman who is next to him, even if there is harm from him that hurts him. This hadith is not narrated from Khidash except with this chain; Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"2453","2450 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Ziyad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is gifted a gift while people are with him, they are partners with him in it. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except Ibn Jurayj; Mindal is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"2454","2451 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni who said: Abd Allah ibn Rabah wrote to me narrating to me from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we sat at the door. He heard two men disputing over a verse, so he came out to us with anger visible on his face, saying: Those before you perished only due to their excessive disputing. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Rabah except Abu Imran al-Jawni; Hammad is alone in transmitting it."
"2455","2452 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into solid ghee, and said: What is beneath it and around it is taken and discarded, then the remainder is eaten. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Said except Mamar, nor narrated it from Mamar except Yazid and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"2456","2453 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Uthman, freedman of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one. No one narrated this hadith from Shayban except Abd Allah."
"2457","2454 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men of those before you went out seeking pasture for their families; rain befell them, so they took shelter at a mountain or a cave, and a rock fell upon them. One of them said to another: The rock has fallen and the trace is effaced, and none knows your place except Allah Almighty; supplicate by your most reliable deeds. One of them said: I had two parents, and I would milk for them in a vessel; when I came to them while they slept I would stand until they awoke whenever they awoke, disliking that drowsiness circulate in their heads; when they awoke they drank. O Allah, if You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. A third of the rock moved. Another said: O Allah, if You know there was a woman who pleased me, and I desired her but she refused to give herself to me until I offered her a reward; when she took her reward and settled herself, I left her. O Allah, if You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. Two thirds of the rock moved. The third said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a laborer to work a day, and he worked, then came seeking his wage, and I gave it to him but he refused it and despised it; so I multiplied it for him until it became of all wealth; then he came seeking his wage, and I said: Take all this; had I wished I would have given him only his wage. O Allah, if You know I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, relieve us. A third of the rock moved, and they walked out. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan except Imran."
"2458","2455 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek help in fulfilling needs through concealment, for every possessor of blessing is envied. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain; Said is alone in transmitting it."
"2459","2456 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I asked Zayd ibn Aslam and he narrated to me from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man was herding a she-camel of his near Uhud, and it presented itself so he slaughtered it with a peg. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Eat it. Jarir said: I said to Zayd: Was the peg of iron or wood? He said: Of wood. This hadith is not narrated from Zayd except through the hadith of Jarir; Habban ibn Hilal narrated this hadith from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Zayd ibn Aslam. Jarir said: Then I met Zayd ibn Aslam and he narrated it to me."
"2460","2457 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Imran ibn Hittan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not leave in his house anything bearing crosses except that he cut it off. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except by Imran."
"2461","2458 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man narrates a narration then turns, it is a trust. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Abd Allah except with this chain; Ibn Abi Dhib is alone in transmitting it."
"2462","2459 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Yazid al-Taghlibi informed us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks in silver vessels only gurgles fire in his belly. No one narrated this hadith from Salim, from Aishah except Sad; Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"2463","2460 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Yazid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Salim, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No vein ever throbs upon a believer except that Allah removes a sin from him by it, writes a good deed for him, and raises a rank for him. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"2464","2461 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sad ibn Iyad, from Ibn Masud who said: The most beloved meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the foreleg of sheep, and we used to think it was the Jews who poisoned him therein. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zuhayr."
"2465","2462 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Ziyad al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mustalim ibn Said narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Maymun, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is an obligation upon every Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Mustalim except Hibban; Malik is alone in transmitting it."
"2466","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, they said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is shown a kindness, let him repay it; if he cannot, let him mention it, for if he mentions it he has thanked for it, and one who feigns satiety with what he did not receive is like one wearing two garments of falsehood. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih."
"2467","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Mamar ibn Abd Allah al-Adawi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None hoards except a sinner. None narrated this hadith from Murajja except Abu Umar al-Hawdi."
"2468","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the leasing of land for cultivation."
"2469","And from Muhammad ibn Sirin, that Hakim ibn Hizam said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what is not in my possession."
"2470","And from Muhammad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and paid the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him."
"2471","And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten the prayer between Madinah and Makkah, fearing none but Allah the Exalted."
"2472","And from Muhammad, that a funeral passed by Ibn Abbas and al-Hasan ibn Ali, and one of them stood while the other remained seated; the one standing said to the one sitting: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand? He said: Yes indeed, and he also sat."
"2473","And from Muhammad, that Abu Said al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a people who recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats; they shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the target, then never return to it."
"2474","And from Muhammad, that Aishah reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray standing and sitting; when he prayed standing he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting."
"2475","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari and Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, they said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters, and I shall strike a parable for you about that: Allah has a protected pasture, and the protected pasture of Allah is what He forbade, and whoever grazes around the pasture is about to enter it."
"2476","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abidah al-Salmani, he said: Shall I not inform you of what Ali informed me? He said: Among them is a man with a deformed arm, or a small arm, or a mutilated arm; were it not that you would become overconfident I would inform you of what Allah has promised those who fight them upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kabah, repeating it three times."
"2477","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu al-Salil, he said: Abu Dharr said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite to me this verse: And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect; and whoever relies upon Allah, He is sufficient for him, and he kept repeating it to me until I dozed. Then he said: O Abu Dharr, what will you do when you are expelled from Madinah? I said: I will go to ease and comfort, I will go and become a dove of the doves of the Sanctuary. He said: What will you do when you are expelled from Makkah? I said: To ease and comfort, to Syria and the Holy Land. He said: What will you do when you are expelled from Syria? I said: Then, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will place my sword upon my shoulder. He said: Or better than that: you hear and obey, even if he is an Abyssinian slave."
"2478","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Kahmas narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the forenoon prayer? She said: No, except when he came from a journey. I said: Did he pray sitting? She said: Yes, after the people had worn him down with age. I said: Did he join surahs together? She said: The Mufassal. I said: Did he fast a whole month? She said: I never knew him to fast a whole month except Ramadan, nor to break fast a whole month until he fasted some of it apart from Ramadan."
"2479","And from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Mihjan ibn al-Adra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand, then he met me as I was going out on the road of Madinah, and he took my hand, and we set out until we climbed Uhud, and he turned toward Madinah and said: Woe to it as a mother, a town whose people will leave it at its most flourishing. I said: O Prophet of Allah, who will eat its fruit? He said: The healthy of birds and beasts, and the Dajjal will not enter it; whenever he intends to enter it, an angel meets him at every pass of its passes and turns him back. Then he turned, until when we were at the door of the mosque there was a man praying, and he said: He says it truthfully. I said: O Prophet of Allah, this is so-and-so, the most prayerful of the people of Madinah. He said: Do not let him hear lest you destroy him."
"2480","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, he said: I said to Abu Said al-Khudri: Dictate to us in writing. He said: Why should we write for you? We will not make it a Quran, but take from us as we used to take from the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And Abu Said used to say: Narrate traditions, for one hadith reminds of another."
"2481","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief. None narrated this hadith from Kahmas except al-Shuaythi."
"2482","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Kahmas narrated to us, from Burd Abu al-Ala, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: I said to Aishah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform witr at the beginning of the night or at its end? She said: Sometimes he performed witr at its beginning and sometimes at its end. I said: Allah is Great, praise be to Allah who has made latitude in the matter. I said: When major impurity befell him, did he bathe at the beginning of the night or at its end? She said: Sometimes he bathed at its beginning and sometimes at its end. I said: Allah is Great, praise be to Allah who has made latitude in the matter. I said: Did he recite aloud in his prayer or softly? She said: Sometimes he recited aloud and sometimes softly. I said: Allah is Great, praise be to Allah who has made latitude in the matter."
"2483","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to fast Ashura. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Lahiah; Muadh is alone in it."
"2484","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from a man, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed some poetry contains wisdom. None narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Awanah; Yahya is alone in it."
"2485","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so extinguish it with water. None narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah except al-Hajabi."
"2486","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to a people who had set up a live pigeon as a target and were shooting at it, and he said: This tied target, its eating is not lawful. None narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr except Muslim."
"2487","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes a handspan of land, Allah will collar him with seven earths."
"2488","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people were the weak and the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people were women. None narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abd Allah except al-Dahhak ibn Yasar."
"2489","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed us, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a boy, and I went early before him and took his hand so that he would pledge allegiance to me, but he returned it and did not pledge me. None narrated this hadith from al-Hirmas except Ikrimah."
"2490","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sacrifice is obligatory upon me, and it is a sunnah for you. None narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Abu Janab."
"2491","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Nasih ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: A young man used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and hasten in his needs, and he said: Ask me for a need. He said: Pray for Paradise for me. He said: He raised his head and breathed, and said: Yes, but help me with abundant prostration."
"2492","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buries three and is patient over them and seeks reward, Paradise becomes due for him. Umm Ayman said: Or two? He said: Whoever buries two and is patient over them and seeks reward, Paradise becomes due for him. Umm Ayman said: And one? He fell silent and held back, then said: O Umm Ayman, whoever buries one and is patient over him and seeks reward, Paradise becomes due for him. None narrated these two hadiths from Simak except Nasih."
"2493","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by sellers of food and saw fine food, and he put his hand into it, and beneath it was inferior food, and he said: Sell this separately and this separately; whoever cheats us is not of us. None narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abu Mashar."
"2494","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, he said: A funeral was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there a debt upon your companion? They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over your companion. A man said: It is upon me, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed over him. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"2495","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Miswar ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the mines of piety is your learning, in addition to what you already know, what you do not know, and falling short in what you know is lack of increase in it, and what makes a man disinterested in the knowledge of what he does not know is only lack of benefiting from what he already knows. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Yasin."
"2496","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani informed them, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you see those who praise excessively, throw dust in their faces. None narrated this hadith from Ata except Ali ibn al-Hakam; Hammad is alone in it."
"2497","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Manzur narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qadariyyah are the Magians of this ummah; if they fall ill do not visit them, and if they die do not attend them. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Zakariyya."
"2498","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at bedtime, for it grows the hair and clears the sight. None narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr except Muslim."
"2499","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Yazid the freedman of al-Munbaith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lost property. He said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it for a year; if its owner comes and recognizes its number and its tie, give it to him, otherwise it is yours. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Hammad."
"2500","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant remains in good so long as he does not hasten. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does he hasten? He said: He says: I supplicated and it was not answered for me. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Hilal."
"2501","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Manzur narrated to us, he said: Attaf al-Shami narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No caution avails against decree, and supplication benefits against what has befallen and what has not befallen, and supplication meets affliction and they contend until the Day of Resurrection. None narrated this hadith from Hisham except Attaf, nor from Attaf except Zakariyya; al-Hajabi is alone in it."
"2502","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he wiped his forehead with his right hand, then said: In the name of Allah besides whom there is no god, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; O Allah, remove from me grief and sorrow. None narrated this hadith from Muawiyah except Zayd; Sallam is alone in it."
"2503","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrating from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, if I coincide with the Night of Decree, what shall I ask Allah? He said: Ask Him for well-being. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hilal except Abu Umar."
"2504","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd Allah, the freedman of Ghufrah, narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Safwan al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has companies of angels who alight and stand over gatherings of remembrance on earth, so go morning and evening in the remembrance of Allah, and remind Allah by yourselves; whoever wishes to know his standing with Allah, let him look at how Allah stands with him, for Allah the Exalted places the servant where he places Him in himself. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Umar is alone in it."
"2505","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who maintain the houses of Allah are the people of Allah the Exalted. None narrated this hadith from Thabit except Salih."
"2506","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Mansur, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know better what is with the Dajjal than he does; with him is a burning fire and a river of cold water, so whoever reaches him must not perish by him; let him close his eyes and fall into what he sees as fire, for it is cool water for them."
"2507","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Najih al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Sinan narrated to us, who is not Dirar, from Imran ibn Wahb, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The screen between the eyes of the jinn and the private parts of the sons of Adam when they remove their clothes is that they say: In the name of Allah. None narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Hajjaj."
"2508","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Ayyub and Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ghallab Yunus ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: Do you know Abd Allah ibn Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he commanded him to take her back. I said: Is it counted against him? He said: Yes; what do you think if he is incapable and foolish. None narrated this hadith from Salamah except Hammad."
"2509","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Sawwar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him it envelops him, and Allah appoints seventy thousand angels to pray for him until evening. None narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Musab ibn Sawwar."
"2510","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man used to sell wine in a ship at sea and used to mix it with water, and with him in the ship was a monkey; the monkey took the money bag and climbed the mast with it, and began dropping a dinar into the ship and a dinar into the water, until it divided it in halves. None narrated this hadith from Abu Salih except Ishaq; Hammad is alone in it."
"2511","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Nuh ibn Hakim narrated to me, and he was a reciter of the Quran, from a man called Dawud, whom Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan bore, from Layla bint Qanif al-Thaqafiyyah, she said: I was among those who washed Umm Kulthum the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The first thing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us was the waist-wrapper, then the shirt, then the head-cover, then the sheet, then she was wrapped in the largest garment. This hadith is not narrated from Layla bint Qanif except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq is alone in it."
"2512","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Maqil ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Ismail al-Bajali narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah al-Thumali, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Fatimah, stand and witness your sacrifice, for you are forgiven for every sin you committed with every drop of its blood, and say: Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds, no partner has He, and with that I am commanded and I am the first of the Muslims. Imran said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for you and your household specifically, for you are worthy of that, or for the Muslims generally? He said: Rather for the Muslims generally. This hadith is not narrated from Imran ibn al-Husayn except with this chain; Abu Hamzah is alone in it."
"2513","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not let his wife enter the bathhouse, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is drunk. None narrated this hadith from Abbad except Hajjaj."
"2514","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, preaching upon the pulpit, saying: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you when you are guided, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people see an evil and do not change it, Allah is about to envelop them all in punishment. None narrated this hadith from Malik except Hajjaj ibn Nusayr."
"2515","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Opening of the Book over funerals. None narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Shaybah."
"2516","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A funeral was brought past the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they spoke well of him, so he said: It has become due. Then another funeral was brought past, and evil was spoken of it, so he said: It has become due. It was said: What has become due? He said: You are the witnesses of Allah on earth, whether for good or for evil. None narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Umar except al-Qanabi."
"2517","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, he said: Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from al-Dahhak ibn Qays al-Fihri, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man comes to a people and they say: Welcome, then welcome to him on the day he meets his Lord, and when a man comes to a people and they say: Misery, then misery to him on the day he meets his Lord. This hadith is not narrated from al-Dahhak ibn Qays except with this chain; Hammad ibn Salamah is alone in it."
"2518","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Rabiah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, he said: A shaykh of the people of Madinah kunya Abu Ayyub narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a funeral was brought and the people spoke well of it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then another was brought, and the people as it were spoke ill of him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So-and-so was brought and he said: It has become due, then so-and-so was brought and he said: It has become due. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard them and said: What is this? Umar said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, so-and-so was brought and the people spoke much good of him, and you said: It has become due, then so-and-so was brought and the people spoke evil of him, and you said: It has become due. He said: Your brother was brought and you testified as you testified, so your testimony became due, then your brother so-and-so was brought and you testified as you testified, so your testimony became due; you are the witnesses of Allah on earth, some of you over others. None narrated this hadith from Abu Ayyub al-Madani except Rabiah ibn Kulthum ibn Jabr."
"2519","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Talhah, he said: I was among those upon whom drowsiness was poured on the day of Uhud."
"2520","And with the same chain, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man in Paradise is given the strength of so-and-so many women. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, can he bear that? He said: He is given the strength of a hundred."
"2521","And with the same chain, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no servant but he has three friends: one friend says: What you spend is yours, and what you withhold is not yours, and that is his wealth; and one friend says: I am with you, but when you come to the gate of the King I leave you, and that is his family and attendants; and one friend says: I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you exit, and that is his deed, and he says: You were the least of the three to me."
"2522","And with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it. None narrated these hadiths from Qatadah except Imran."
"2523","And from Imran, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"2524","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is in prayer so long as he remains in his place of prayer in which he prayed, as long as he does not break his ablution. None narrated this hadith from Bakr except Imran."
"2525","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said about the Night of Decree: A night of the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth; the angels on that night on earth are more than the number of stars."
"2526","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Nothing is more honored to Allah the Exalted than supplication."
"2527","And from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar al-Mujashii, he said: I gave a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Have you become Muslim? He said: No. He said: I have been forbidden the butter of the polytheists, and he returned it."
"2528","And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two who revile each other, what they say is upon the one who began, unless the wronged one transgresses."
"2529","And with the same chain, from Iyad ibn Himar, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man reviles me, shall I revile him? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two who revile are two devils accusing and belying each other."
"2530","And from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Yemen and said: O Allah, turn their hearts, and bless for us our sa and our mudd."
"2531","And from Qatadah, from Nasr ibn Asim, from Muawiyah al-Laythi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People wake in drought, then Allah brings them provision from Him, and they wake as polytheists, saying: We were rained upon by such-and-such star."
"2532","And from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbih, from Abu Iyad, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of despised deeds, for they gather upon a man until they destroy him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a parable for them like a people who alighted in a barren land, and the need of the people for cooking came, so one man brought such-and-such and another brought a small stick, until they gathered much blackness of that, then kindled a fire, and it cooked what was thrown into it."
"2533","And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the sermon: Praise be to Allah, we seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls; whoever Allah guides none can misguide, and whoever He misguides none can guide, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger is guided, and whoever disobeys them harms only himself and will not harm Allah at all. None narrated these hadiths from Qatadah except Imran."
"2534","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) feared a people he said: O Allah, we place You in their throats and seek refuge in You from their evils."
"2535","And from Qatadah, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Paradise is a brick of gold and a brick of silver."
"2536","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah restored Ayyub, He rained upon him locusts of gold, and he began taking them with his hand and placing them in his garment, and it was said to him: O Ayyub, are you not sated? He said: And who is sated with Your mercy. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hammam."
"2537","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah sent down no disease but He sent down for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it, except al-sam. It was said: And what is al-sam? He said: Death. None narrated this hadith from Ata from Abu Said except Shabib."
"2538","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ribi ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Umm Sulaym visiting her, and she would present to him something she made for him, and I had a small brother kunya Abu Umayr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day and said: O Umm Sulaym, why do I see your son heavy in spirit? She said: O Messenger of Allah, his little bird with which he used to play has died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to say: O Abu Umayr, what did the little bird do?"
"2539","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ribi ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Jarud narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, he said: al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he traveled and wished to perform voluntary prayer, he faced his camel toward the qiblah, said takbir, then prayed wherever it turned. These two hadiths are not narrated from al-Jarud except with this chain; Ribi is alone in them."
"2540","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Maqil ibn Malik al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jammaz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love of Quraysh is faith and hatred of them is disbelief, and love of the Arabs is faith and hatred of them is disbelief; whoever loves the Arabs has loved me, and whoever hates the Arabs has hated me. None narrated this hadith from Thabit except al-Haytham."
"2541","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hammad al-Shuaythi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two evening prayers, praying two rakahs then giving salam, then went to a log laid across, and the hasty ones exited the mosque saying: The prayer has been shortened. Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and they were awed to speak to him. Among the people was a man called Dhu al-Yadayn, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, did you forget or has the prayer been shortened? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I neither forgot nor was the prayer shortened. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says? They said: Yes. He came and prayed what remained upon him, then gave salam, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, and raised his head, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer. It was said to him: Did he give salam? He said: I was informed that Imran ibn Husayn said: He gave salam."
"2542","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ararah ibn al-Birind narrated to us, he said: Faddal ibn al-Zubayr ibn Jabir, Abu Muhannad al-Ghudani, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah Sudayy ibn Ajlan al-Bahili say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guarantee for me six things and I guarantee Paradise for you: when one of you speaks let him not lie, and when he promises let him not break it, and when he is entrusted let him not betray, and lower your gazes, and guard your private parts, and restrain your hands."
"2543","And with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, whoever has them finds the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger be more beloved to him than all else, and that he love a servant loving him only for Allah, and that being thrown into the Fire be more beloved to him than returning to disbelief after Allah saved him from it."
"2544","And with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, come to your Lord; what is little and suffices is better than what is much and distracts. O people, there are but two paths: a path of good and a path of evil, so why do you make the path of evil more beloved to you than the path of good?"
"2545","And with the same chain, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, fear the Fire even with half a date."
"2546","And with the same chain, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a Muslim? He said: One from whose tongue the Muslims are safe. These hadiths are not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Faddal is alone in them."
"2547","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Ata narrated to me, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold he would seek a third to them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."
"2548","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold and wore it three days, and gold rings spread among his companions, so he threw it away and took a ring of silver, engraving upon it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. It was in his hand until he died, and in the hand of Abu Bakr until he died, and in the hand of Umar until he died, and in the hand of Uthman six years; when writings upon him became many he gave it to a man of the Ansar to seal with, and he came to a well of Uthman and it fell into it, and they searched for it but did not find it, so he took a ring of silver and engraved upon it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"2549","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Shubah."
"2550","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Dubaah bint al-Zubayr: Perform hajj and stipulate: My release is where You detain me. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Hisham."
"2551","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Rufay Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Trustworthy men narrated to me, among them Umar, and the most pleasing of them to me was Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and prayer after Asr until the sun sets. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hilal except Abu Umar."
"2552","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Nafi, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his camel stood upright with him."
"2553","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued talbiyah on the Day of Sacrifice until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. None narrated this hadith from Qays except Hammad."
"2554","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim al-Kulaybi narrated to us, he said: Zaidah ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Rifaah al-Qitbani, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man grants a man security over his blood then kills him except that the killer is free of the killed."
"2555","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut for a shield. I said to Anas: What was its price? He said: Five dirhams. Abu Hilal said: Said ibn Abi Arubah differs with me, saying: It is from Abu Bakr. I met Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, and he said: It is from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"2556","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abza, from Abu Bakr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back Maiz ibn Malik three times. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; Jabir al-Jufi is alone in it."
"2557","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Maiz came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed adultery, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Perhaps you kissed or touched or felt. He said: No. He said: Did you do such-and-such, without euphemism? He said: Yes. He commanded regarding him and he was stoned. None narrated this hadith from Yala except Jarir."
"2558","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mutarrif and Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I asked Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides the Quran? He said: No, by the One who split the seed and created the soul, except that Allah the Exalted grants understanding in His Book, or what is in the sheet. I said: And what is in the sheet? He said: Blood-money and freeing the captive, and that no Muslim be killed for a disbeliever. None narrated this hadith from Ismail except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; al-Ramadi is alone in it."
"2559","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hawshab ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Mahdi al-Hajari, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Arafah at Arafah. None narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Mahdi; Hawshab is alone in it."
"2560","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Razin narrated to us, he said: My mother narrated to me, she said: Umm al-Harir, when an Arab man died, grieved intensely. It was said to her: O Umm al-Harir, why is it that when an Arab man dies you grieve intensely? She said: I heard my master say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the approach of the Hour is the perishing of the Arabs. Muhammad ibn Razin said: Her master was Talhah ibn Malik. This hadith is not narrated from Talhah ibn Malik except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Harb is alone in it."
"2561","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought milk on the day of Arafah, and he drank and gave drink to the one on his right. None narrated this hadith from Jabir except Sharik."
"2562","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, he said: al-Saq ibn Hazn narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Uthman ibn Umayr, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, he said: The two sons of Mulaykah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, our mother used to guard the husband and honor the guest, and she died in ignorance; where is our mother? He said: Your mother is in the Fire. They rose with distress upon them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them, and they returned, and he said: My mother is with your mother. A man of the hypocrites said: And what avails this for his mother, while we tread his heels? An Ansari man, a youth, I never saw a man who asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than him, said: O Messenger of Allah, where is your father? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord the Exalted for them, and I shall stand the Praiseworthy Station. None narrated this hadith from Abu Wail except Uthman; al-Saq is alone in it."
"2563","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Maymun Abu Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) describing olive oil and wars for pleurisy. Qatadah said: It is poured from the side he complains of. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; his son Muadh is alone in it."
"2564","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: Murajja ibn Raja narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Arzami, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: I bought two brother slaves, and I wished to sell one of them and keep the other, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me, saying: Sell them both together and keep them both together. None narrated this hadith from Murajja except al-Hawdi."
"2565","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Abu Tamimah al-Tamimi, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts the whole age, Allah constricts Hell upon him like this, and he joined his fingers upon ninety."
"2566","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Awdh Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at a house in which were a group of Quraysh, and he took the two doorposts, then said: Is there in the house any but a Qurashi? They said: No, except a sister's son of ours. He said: The sister's son of a people is of them. Then he said: This matter shall remain in Quraysh so long as, when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, and when they judge they are just, and when they divide they are equitable; whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; neither exchange nor ransom is accepted from him. None narrated this hadith from Awf except Muadh ibn Awdh Allah, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain."
"2567","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No disposal by a woman in her wealth is allowed when her husband owns her bond. None narrated this hadith from Dawud except Hammad."
"2568","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah: Do not ask for leadership, for if you are given it upon asking you will be entrusted to it, and if you are given it without asking you will be aided in it, and when you swear an oath and see another better than it, expiate your oath and do what is better."
"2569","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Qays ibn al-Sakan, he said: I was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Masud on the day of Ashura, and before him was a bowl of tharid, and al-Ashath ibn Qays entered, and he said: Come to lunch, O Abu Muhammad. He said: Have you not fasted this day? Abd Allah said: We used to fast it before Ramadan was revealed; when Ramadan was revealed we fasted it and left what was besides it."
"2570","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, he said: Yahya ibn Hind ibn Harithah narrated to me, from his uncle Asma ibn Harithah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me saying: Go to your people and command them to fast this day, meaning the day of Ashura. I said: I do not see myself reaching them except that they will have eaten. He said: Command them to fast the rest of their day."
"2571","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ulaylah bint al-Kumayt al-Atakiyyah narrated to us, she said: I heard my mother Munyah narrating from Amat Allah the daughter of Razinah, whose mother was a servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard my mother Razinah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to magnify the day of Ashura, so much that he would call his children and the suckling children of Fatimah, and say to their mothers: Do not nurse them till night, and he would spit in their mouths, and his saliva sufficed them."
"2572","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Yasin ibn Hammad al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the saying of Allah the Exalted: Not equal are those of the believers who sit, other than those of harm, he said: They were a people in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who did not go out to battle with him due to illnesses and pains and diseases, and others were healthy, and the sick were more excused than the healthy. None narrated this hadith from Abu Nadrah except Abu Aqil al-Dawraqi: Bashir ibn Uqbah."
"2573","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Bannah al-Juhani informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a people handling an unsheathed sword, and said: Allah curse whoever does this; did I not forbid this?"
"2574","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father, he said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mutim say: On the day of Hunayn I saw a black thing like a cloak between heaven and earth, and when it pressed to the earth it spread upon the earth as dust, and the polytheists were defeated. This hadith is not narrated from Jubayr ibn Mutim except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq is alone in it."
"2575","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Muhammad al-Sirini narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Bilal and found with him a heap of dates, and said: What is this, O Bilal? He said: Dates I stored for you. He said: Woe to you, O Bilal, do you not fear that it will have vapor in the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear decrease from the Owner of the Throne."
"2576","And with the same chain, Abu Hurayrah said: Three my friend Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me which I shall never leave: fasting three days of every month, bathing on Friday, and not sleeping except upon witr. None narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Awn except Bakkar ibn Muhammad."
"2577","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Recite the Quran, and when you recite it do not seek abundance by it, nor be excessive in it, nor turn away from it, nor eat by it. And he said: Women are the people of the Fire. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers and sisters and daughters? He mentioned their ingratitude for the right of the husband and their neglect of his right. None narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Wuhayb."
"2578","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which sin is greatest? He said: That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you. I said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child fearing he will eat with you. I said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with the wife of your neighbor. Then he recited: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah forbade except with right, nor commit adultery. None narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Wasil except Muhammad ibn Kathir and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"2579","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that Muadh ibn Jabal used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come and pray with his people. None narrated this hadith from Hisham except Hajjaj."
"2580","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Trustworthy men testified before me, and the most pleasing of them to me was Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham."
"2581","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not boast of your fathers who died in ignorance, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than your fathers who died in ignorance. None narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hisham, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, and al-Hasan al-Qafilani."
"2582","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah ibn Yala al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that a building be ennobled for him and degrees raised for him, let him pardon whoever wronged him, and give whoever deprived him, and join whoever cut him. None narrated this hadith from Musa except Abu Umayyah; Hajjaj is alone in it, and it is not narrated from Ubayy ibn Kab except with this chain."
"2583","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: al-Yaman ibn al-Mughirah al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, that Mujahid informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As, he said: I came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among some of his companions, among them Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and I caught the end of the hadith, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays four rakahs before Asr, the Fire shall not touch him. I said with my hand like this, moving my hand: This is a good hadith. Umar ibn al-Khattab said to me: What you missed of the beginning of the hadith is better and better. I said: O Ibn al-Khattab, then give it. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah shall enter Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr from Umar except with this chain; Hajjaj is alone in it."
"2584","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves that His concessions be acted upon as He loves that His strict commands be acted upon. None narrated this hadith raised from Shubah except Mamar and Miskin ibn Bukayr al-Harrani."
"2585","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghadirah Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ghadban ibn Hanzalah narrated to me, from his father Hanzalah ibn Nuaym al-Anazi, he said: I was among those who came as a delegation to Umar, and he began asking man by man: From whom are you? And who are you? Until he reached me, and said: From whom are you? And who are you? I said: I am Hanzalah, of Anazah. He gestured toward the east and spread his fingers, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Anazah is a tribe from here, wronged yet aided. This hadith was not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Abu Ghadirah is alone in it."
"2586","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from al-Ajlah ibn Abd Allah al-Kindi, from Adi ibn Adi al-Kindi, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at an hour other than that in which he used to come to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to him and said: O Jibril, why do I see you changed in color? He said: I did not come to you until Allah the Exalted commanded the keys of the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jibril, describe to me the Fire and depict for me Jahannam. Jibril said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded Jahannam and it was kindled a thousand years until it whitened, then He commanded and it was kindled a thousand years until it reddened, then He commanded and it was kindled a thousand years until it blackened, and it is black, dark, its spark does not give light and its flame is not extinguished. By the One who sent you with the truth, if the measure of a needle hole were opened from Jahannam, all upon earth would die together from its heat. By the One who sent you with the truth, if a garment of the garments of the Fire were hung between heaven and earth, all upon earth would die from its heat. By the One who sent you with the truth, if a keeper of the keepers of Jahannam emerged to the people of the world and they looked at him, all upon earth would die from the ugliness of his face and the foulness of his smell. By the One who sent you with the truth, if a ring of the rings of the chain of the people of the Fire which Allah described in His Book were placed upon the mountains of the world, they would crumble and not come together until reaching the lowest earth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough, O Jibril, lest my heart burst and I die. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Jibril while he wept, and said: Do you weep, O Jibril, while you are with Allah in the station you are in? He said: And why should I not weep? I am most worthy of weeping, lest I be in the knowledge of Allah upon other than the state I am upon, and I do not know, lest I be tried as Iblis was tried, for he was of the angels, and what assures me lest I be tried as Harut and Marut were tried. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept, and Jibril, peace be upon him, wept, and they kept weeping until they were called: O Jibril and O Muhammad, Allah the Exalted has secured you from disobeying Him. Jibril, peace be upon him, ascended, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and passed by a people of the Ansar laughing and playing, and said: Do you laugh while behind you is Jahannam? If you knew what I know you would laugh little and weep much, and food and drink would not be pleasant to you, and you would go out to the open roads crying out to Allah the Exalted. He was called: O Muhammad, do not despair My servants; I sent you as a facilitator and did not send you as a complicator. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright and draw near. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Sallam is alone in it."
"2587","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not take for you something at Mina in which you may shade? He said: O Aishah, Mina is but the camping place of whoever precedes. None narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Israil."
"2588","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father, he said: We said: We know how to greet you, so how do we pray upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. This hadith is not narrated from Talhah except from the hadith of Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, and none narrated it from Uthman except Israil and Sharik."
"2589","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Yahya al-Ushnani narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The best of us after our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2590","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: Shall I not gift you a gift I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? I said: Yes. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we know greeting you, so how do we pray upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"2591","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Waqid al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Malik, he said: al-Bara ibn Azib said: While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he saw a group of people, and said: Upon what have these gathered? It was said: Upon a grave they are digging. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was startled and hastened before his companions until he reached the grave, and he threw soil upon it, and faced from before it, and wept, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until he moistened the soil with his tears, then turned to us and said: My brothers, for the like of this day prepare. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain; Abd Allah ibn Waqid is alone in it."
"2592","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, he said: al-Bara ibn Azib narrated to us, he said: We were in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing they waited until they saw him prostrated with his forehead placed upon the ground. None narrated this hadith from Jarir except Arim."
"2593","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsajah, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a grant of silver, or gives milk to drink, or guides a lane, it equals a neck, and whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Capable, ten times, it equals a neck. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us wiping our shoulders and chests, saying: Let not your rows differ lest your hearts differ; Allah the Exalted and His angels pray upon the first rows. None narrated this hadith from Zubayd except Jarir."
"2594","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abidah, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which people are best? He said: My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then comes a people whose one's testimony precedes his oath and his oath his testimony."
"2595","And with the same chain, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the captive."
"2596","And with the same chain, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none but a companion from the jinn entrusted to him. They said: And you? He said: And me, but Allah the Exalted aided me over him so he submitted, and he commands me only with good."
"2597","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Maysarah al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Dalani narrated to me, from Abu Yahya, the freedman of the family of Jadah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril took my hand and showed me the gate of Paradise through which my ummah shall enter. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I wished I were with you to see it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are the first of my ummah to enter Paradise."
"2598","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wretched is the slave of the dinar, wretched is the slave of the dirham, wretched is the slave of the fine garment; if given he is pleased, and if withheld he is angry; wretched and relapsed, and when pricked let him not be extracted. Blessed is a servant taking the bridle of his horse in the path of Allah, his head disheveled, his feet dusty; if guarding, he is in guarding, and if in the rear, he is in the rear; if he intercedes he is not interceded for, and if he seeks permission he is not permitted."
"2599","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Musa Abu Utbah al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Matar ibn Ukamis, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah the Exalted decrees for a man to die in a land, He makes for him therein a need."
"2600","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Mawraq al-Ijli, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man in congregation exceeds his prayer by twenty-five degrees. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Mawraq, except Hammam."
"2601","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi informed us, from Awn ibn Abd Allah, from his brother Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a black slave girl, and said: Upon me is a believing neck. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Who is your Lord? She pointed to the heaven and said: Allah. He said: Who am I? She said: His Messenger, gesturing with her hand to the earth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Free her, for she is a believer. None narrated this hadith from Awn except al-Masudi."
"2602","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Israil informed us, from Muslim al-Awar, from Habbah al-Urani, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to eat garlic, saying: Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would eat it."
"2603","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah at Khaybar with fighting severe, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah is Great, Khaybar is opened, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"2604","And from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The people of Madinah were struck by drought and severe famine, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit preaching on Friday, and people stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished, and we fear perishing upon ourselves, and prices rose and rain was withheld; pray to Allah to give us drink. Anas said: I saw no whiteness in the sky, and he extended his hand, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and prayed; by Allah, he had not joined his hand to him until I saw clouds coming from here and here, and they became heaped, then it rained seven days, until by Allah a young man would intend to return to his family from the severity of the rain. When the next Friday came and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preached, people stood from the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed and roads are cut; pray to Allah to withhold it from us. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smile, and he raised his hands and said: Around us and not upon us. Anas said: I saw no greenness in the sky, and by Allah, he had not lowered his hand until I saw the sky splitting here and here from Madinah, and morning came while around it were pools. None narrated these two hadiths from Imran al-Qattan except Abd Allah ibn Raja."
"2605","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once sent a man to a man of the pharaohs of the Arabs, saying: Call him to me. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is more defiant than that. He said: Go to him and call him. He came to him and said to him: The Messenger of Allah calls you. He said: Messenger of Allah! What is Allah? Is He of gold, or of silver, or of copper? He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, saying: I told you, O Messenger of Allah, that he is more defiant than that. He said: Return to him and call him. He came to him and repeated the first saying to him, and he repeated to him the like of his first answer. He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return to him and call him. He returned to him the third time, and while they exchanged speech between them, Allah the Exalted sent a cloud over his head, and it thundered and lightened, and a thunderbolt fell from it taking the crown of his head, and Allah the Exalted revealed: And He sends thunderbolts striking with them whom He wills while they dispute about Allah, and He is Mighty in assault. None narrated this hadith from Thabit except Ali ibn Abi Sarah."
"2606","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd Abu Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sealed scrolls shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection and set before Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, shall say: Cast these and accept these. The angels shall say: By Your might, we saw only good. Allah the Exalted shall say: This was for other than My face, and I accept today from deeds only what was sought for My face. None narrated this hadith from Abu Imran except al-Harith ibn Ubayd."
"2607","Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Kashshi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us, he said: Ghalib ibn Hajrah narrated to us, he said: Umm Abd Allah the daughter of Milqam narrated to me, from her father Milqam, from his grandfather al-Tilibb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, and what exceeds is charity. This hadith is not narrated from al-Tilibb except with this chain; Ghalib ibn Hajrah is alone in it."
"2608","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see a man seeking a lost item in the mosque, say: May you not find it, and when you see him selling in the mosque, say: May Allah not profit your trade. None narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Khusayfah connected in chain except al-Darawardi."
"2609","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us except saying: No faith for one with no trust, and no religion for one with no covenant."
"2610","Abu Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Harith narrated to us, he said: Tarif ibn Isa al-Anbari narrated to me, he said: Yusuf ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: I met Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for his household, mentioning Ali and Fatimah and others. I said: O Messenger of Allah, am I of the household? He said: Yes, so long as you do not stand at the door of a dais, or come to a ruler asking him. None narrated this hadith from Tarif except Khalid."
"2611","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Sumayyah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upset with Safiyyah over something, so Safiyyah said to me: Will you reconcile the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me, and my day will be yours? So I wore a veil of mine that was dyed with saffron, and sprinkled it with water, then I came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Keep away from me, for it is not your day. So I said: That is the bounty of Allah which He gives to whom He wills, and I told him the story, and he became pleased with her."
"2612","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Sumayyah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and we were with him, when a camel belonging to Safiyyah fell ill, while Zaynab had extra mounts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: The camel of Safiyyah has fallen ill, so if only you would give her one of your camels. She said: Should I give this Jewess? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and boycotted her for the rest of Dhu al-Hijjah, and Muharram, and Safar, and some days of the month of Rabi al-Awwal, until she removed her belongings and her bed, thinking that he had no need of her. Then while she was one day sitting at midday, she saw his shadow approaching, so she put back her bed and her belongings. No one narrated these two hadiths from Thabit except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"2613","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, saying: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Abu Shihab."
"2614","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim informed us, from his father, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: The Quran was revealed that nothing prohibits except ten known sucklings or five known ones. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Hammad."
"2615","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you say: My soul has become wicked, but let him say: My soul has become heavy. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Hajjaj."
"2616","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan, and Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Ghanawi narrated to us, saying, regarding the sermon of Utbah ibn Ghazwan at Basra: Beware, this world has announced its parting and turned away swiftly; beware, nothing remains of it except a dreg like the dreg of a vessel which one of you pours out; beware, you are inevitably moving on from it, so move on with the best of what is at your disposal; beware, I was once the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we had no food except tree leaves, until our mouths were ulcerated; and we woke up with every one of us a commander; and I remember myself with seven others when we found a cloak and split it among us; beware, it is astonishing that a great rock is thrown into Hellfire and falls down seventy autumns without reaching its bottom; beware, it is astonishing that the distance between the two doorposts of the gates of Paradise is forty days, yet a day will come upon it when it is crowded with throngs. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Sahl."
"2617","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that a man from the desert people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer. So he indicated with his finger like this: Two by two, and the witr is one rakah at the end of the night."
"2618","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House in the year of the Conquest upon his mount, touching the Corner with his staff. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except al-Darawardi."
"2619","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid prayer without adhan or iqamah, then delivered the sermon after the prayer, then came to the women with Bilal, stood over them and urged them to give charity, and how many rings and necklaces were thrown into the garment of Bilal, until his garment was filled. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Abu Awanah; Abu Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"2620","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The killing of a believer, wronged, defending his wealth, is martyrdom."
"2621","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam in his wall. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Said, except Mamar."
"2622","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Ala al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from Salih ibn Sarj, from Imran ibn Hittan, who said: We entered upon Aishah, and they mentioned judgeship, so Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The just judge will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and will face such severity of reckoning that he will wish he had never judged between two people even over a date. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Ala was alone in transmitting it."
"2623","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu Musa, in marfu form, who said: He is not of us who shaves the head in grief, tears the garment, and raises the voice in wailing. No one narrates this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Abu Awanah."
"2624","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abu Layla Abdullah ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Mazidah ibn Jabir, from his mother, that Abu Musa said on the day of Ashura: Fast this day, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to fast it. No one narrated this hadith from Mazidah except Abdullah ibn Maysarah."
"2625","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yala Zunbur narrated to us, saying: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nafi, from his father, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qunut in the dawn prayer. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yala was alone in transmitting it."
"2626","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, saying: Ammar Abu Hashim, the saffron merchant, narrated to us, from Salih ibn Ubayd, from Qabisah ibn Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer past its times; it counts for you and against them, so pray with them as long as they pray the prayer for you. This hadith is not narrated from Qabisah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi except with this chain; Abu Hashim was alone in transmitting it."
"2627","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, saying: Al-Muhajir Abu Makhlad narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Muslim al-Judhami, that he heard Abu Dharr say: I said: O Prophet of Allah, which part of the night is most beloved to you if it is decreed for me to pray two rakahs in it? He said: The middle of the night, and few are those who do it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Muslim except Abu al-Ala; al-Muhajir was alone in transmitting it."
"2628","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Babi al-Makki, who said: I prayed beside Ibn Umar, and when he prayed he struck my thigh with his hand and said: Shall I not teach you the greeting of prayer as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us? And he recited these words: Greetings, prayers, and good things belong to Allah; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Aban; Sahl was alone in transmitting it."
"2629","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, saying: Wasil, the freed slave of Abu Uyaynah, informed us, from Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah al-Asadi, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: Establishing the prayer at its time. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Mahdi."
"2630","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, saying: Hammam informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed there is in Friday an hour which no Muslim servant meets while asking Allah for good except that He gives it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammam except Abdullah ibn Raja."
"2631","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn Atiyyah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and the prayer is established, begin with supper. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hammad."
"2632","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah al-Laythi, then al-Sami al-Nakhai, narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayf, from his father, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, so I went out to him and found him feverish with his head bandaged. He said: Take my hand, O Fadl. So I took his hand until he reached the pulpit and sat upon it, then he said to me: Call out among the people. So I called out among the people, and they gathered to him. He praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and extolled Him, then said: O people, claims owed by me from among you have drawn near; whoever I have flogged on his back, here is my back, let him retaliate from it; and whoever I have insulted in his honor, here is my honor, let him retaliate from it; and whoever I have taken wealth from, here is my wealth, let him retaliate from it; and let no man say: I fear hatred from the Messenger of Allah; indeed hatred is not of my nature nor of my character; indeed the most beloved of you to me is he who takes a right if there is one, or absolves me, so that I meet Allah with a content soul; indeed I do not see that as availing me until I stand among you repeatedly. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended and prayed Zhuhr, then returned to the pulpit and repeated his statement about hatred and other matters, then said: O people, whoever has something with him, let him return it, and let him not say: the disgrace of this world; indeed the disgrace of this world is better than the disgrace of the Hereafter. Then a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have three dirhams owed to me by you. He said: We neither belie a claimant nor make him swear an oath, so how did it come to be owed to you by me? He said: Do you remember the day a beggar passed by you and you commanded me, so I gave him three dirhams? He said: Give them to him, O Fadl. Then another man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have three dirhams which I misappropriated from the path of Allah. He said: And why did you misappropriate them? He said: I was in need of them. He said: Take them from him, O Fadl. Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you fears something, let him stand so I may supplicate for him. Then a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a liar, and I am indeed a hypocrite, and I am indeed sleepy. He said: O Allah, grant him truthfulness and faith, and remove sleep from him when he intends. Then a man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a liar and I am indeed a hypocrite, and there is nothing of things except that I have committed it. So Umar said: Fellow, you have disgraced yourself. He said: Stop, O Ibn al-Khattab; the disgrace of this world is easier than the disgrace of the Hereafter; O Allah, grant him truthfulness and faith, and turn his affair to good. Then Umar spoke a word, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar is with me and I am with Umar, and the truth after me is with Umar wherever he is. This hadith is not narrated from al-Fadl except with this chain; al-Harith ibn Abd al-Malik was alone in transmitting it."
"2633","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he hears the striking of their sandals when they turn away from him. If he was a believer, the prayer is at his head, zakah at his right, fasting at his left, and acts of good, kindness, and beneficence to people from the direction of his feet. He is approached from the direction of his head, and the prayer says: There is no entry from my side. Then he is approached from his right, and zakah says: There is no entry from my side. Then he is approached from his left, and fasting says: There is no entry from my side. Then he is approached from the direction of his feet, and acts of good, kindness, and beneficence to people say: There is no entry from my side. Then it is said to him: Sit. So he sits with the sun having been made to appear to him as setting. Then it is said to him: What do you say about this man who was among you? Meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He says: I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah; he came to us with clear proofs from our Lord, so we believed and followed. Then it is said to him: You have spoken the truth; upon this you lived, upon this you died, and upon this you will be resurrected, Allah willing. His grave is widened for him as far as his sight. That is the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. Then it is said: Open for him a door to the Fire. A door to the Fire is opened for him, and it is said: This would have been your abode had you disobeyed Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So he increases in joy and happiness. And it is said to him: Open for him a door to Paradise. So it is opened for him, and it is said: This is your abode and what Allah has prepared for you. So he increases in joy and happiness. The skin is returned to what it began from, and his soul is placed in the spirit of a bird that feeds upon the trees of Paradise. As for the disbeliever, he is approached in his grave from the direction of his head, and nothing is found; then he is approached from the direction of his feet and nothing is found. He sits fearful and terrified. It is said to him: What do you say about this man who was among you? And what do you testify? He cannot recall his name, so it is said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He says: I heard people saying something, so I said as they said. It is said to him: You have spoken the truth; upon this you lived, upon this you died, and upon this you will be resurrected, Allah willing. His grave is constricted upon him until his ribs interlock. That is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: And whoever turns away from My remembrance, indeed for him is a constrained life. Then it is said: Open for him a door to Paradise. A door to Paradise is opened for him, and it is said to him: This would have been your abode and what Allah prepared for you had you obeyed Him. So he increases in regret and loss. Then it is said to him: Open for him a door to the Fire. It is opened for him to it, and it is said to him: This is your abode and what Allah has prepared for you. So he increases in regret and loss. Abu Umar said: I said to Hammad ibn Salamah: Was this one of the people of the qiblah? He said: Yes. Abu Umar said: As if he testifies this testimony without certainty returning to his heart; he used to hear people saying something and would say it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr in its entirety except Hammad ibn Salamah; Abu Umar al-Darir was alone in transmitting it."
"2634","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Rabiah ibn Kulthum ibn Jabr narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to address us at Kufah, saying: The wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is fortunate in his mother's womb. So Hudhayfah ibn Asid, a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: How strange is the affair of this one, saying: The fortunate is he who is fortunate in his mother's womb, and the wretched is he who is wretched in his mother's womb. So Abdullah said: O Hudhayfah, what astonishes you about this? Then he said: Shall I not narrate to you the cure for that? Then he raised the hadith, saying: An angel is entrusted with the womb; when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends to create something by Allah's permission, he says: O Lord, his term. So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: O Lord, his provision. So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. Then he says: Wretched or fortunate? So your Lord decrees and the angel writes. So it is thus, neither more nor less. No one raised this hadith from Rabiah except Muslim."
"2635","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muslim narrated to us, saying: Rabiah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, that he heard al-Hasan say: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me three things: Bathing on Friday, witr before sleep, and fasting three days of every month."
"2636","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Hakkam narrated to us, saying: Al-Muthanna ibn Said al-Qasir narrated to us, saying: Abu Jamrah narrated to us, that Ibn Abbas narrated to them about the beginning of the Islam of Abu Dharr, saying: When it reached him that a man had emerged in Makkah claiming to be a prophet, he sent his brother and said: Go until you bring me news of him and what you hear from him. So his brother went until he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then returned to Abu Dharr and told him that he commands good and forbids evil, and commands noble morals. So Abu Dharr said: You have not satisfied me. So he took a waterskin containing his water and provisions. Then he set out until he came to Makkah, being afraid to ask anyone about anything, and he did not meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He entered the mosque and wandered in it until evening. When night fell, Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by him and said: Who is the man? He said: A man from Ghifar. He said: Come to the dwelling. So he went with him, neither one asking his companion about anything. When morning came, Abu Dharr went out seeking, and when evening came he slept in the mosque. Ali ibn Abi Talib passed by him and said: It is time for the man to know his dwelling. When it was the third day, Ali took a pledge from him that if he told him his affair he would conceal it and keep it secret from him. So he told him that it had reached him that a man had emerged in Makkah claiming to receive revelation, so he sent his brother, but he did not bring him what would satisfy him, so he came himself. Ali said to him: I am going in the morning, so follow me; if I see something I fear for you, I will stand as if pouring water. So Ali went in the morning and Abu Dharr followed behind him, until he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Dharr entered behind him. He informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him, and embraced Islam. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with your command. He said: Return to your people until news of me reaches you. He said: By Allah, I will not return until I proclaim Islam openly. So he went to the mosque and stood shouting at the top of his voice: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. The polytheists said: The man has apostatized. Then they rose to him and beat him until he fell. Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib passed by him, bent over him, and said: You have killed the man, O assembly of Quraysh; you are merchants and your route is through Ghifar; do you wish the road to be cut off? So they refrained from him. The next day he returned to his statement, so they leapt upon him and beat him until he fell. Al-Abbas passed by him, bent over him, and said to them as he had said the day before. So they refrained from him. This was the beginning of the Islam of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jamrah except al-Muthanna, and no one narrated it from al-Muthanna except Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Amr ibn Hakkam."
"2637","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, or Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to address us and remind us of the days of Allah until we could recognize that in his face, as if he were a man fearing that the affair would befall them in the morning. And when he had recently been with Jibril (peace be upon him), he would not smile laughing until it was lifted from him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Hisham."
"2638","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus. He said: There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for it is but decree. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, except Ibrahim. And Malik ibn Anas and the companions of al-Zuhri narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Said."
"2639","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Hisham; Muslim was alone in transmitting it."
"2640","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Waki ibn Udus, from his uncle Abu Razin al-Uqayli, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like the bee; it eats only what is good and produces only what is good. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Hajjaj and Muammal ibn Ismail."
"2641","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ibrahim, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left likewise, until his cheek appeared to them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except al-Hajjaj; Hisham was alone in transmitting it."
"2642","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: Al-Fadl was older than me, and he used to let me ride behind him, so I would be in front of him. I mounted with my brother upon a she-donkey, and we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying with the people at Arafah. We dismounted before him, entered, prayed, and left it grazing before him, and he did not interrupt his prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, except Ismail."
"2643","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) auctioned a mat and a cup, asking who would bid more. A man gave him one dirham, and another gave two dirhams, so he sold it. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Abu Bakr; al-Akhdar was alone in transmitting it."
"2644","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Waqqas ibn Rabiah, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats a meal at the expense of his brother, Allah will feed him its like from the fire of Hell. This hadith is not narrated from al-Mustawrid except with this chain; Sulayman was alone in transmitting it."
"2645","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Rifaa, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it."
"2646","And that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed every treacherous one has a banner on the Day of Resurrection, by which his treachery is known."
"2647","And from Muhammad ibn Rifaa, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when the sun sets: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, nothing will harm him in his night. No one narrated these hadiths from Muhammad ibn Rifaa except Abu Asim."
"2648","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his socks. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qays except Sufyan."
"2649","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold and wore it for three days, then gold rings became widespread, so he threw it away and took a ring of silver, engraving in it: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Abu Asim."
"2650","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Masud narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abu Zumayl Simak ibn al-Walid al-Hanafi, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, for he has disbelieved. He said: And what do you know, O Ibn al-Khattab; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Zumayl, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, except with this chain; Ikrimah was alone in transmitting it."
"2651","Abu Muslim narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Ziyad al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yala Zunbur narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Subh, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was narrating to us at the door of the chambers, Abu Bakr and Umar approached with a crowd of people, answering one another and refuting one another. When they saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they fell silent. He said: What speech did I hear just now, with some of you answering others and some refuting others? A man said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr claimed that good deeds are from Allah and evil deeds are from the servants, while Umar said: Evil deeds and good deeds are from Allah. Some people followed this one and some followed that one, answering and refuting one another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Bakr and said: How did you say? He repeated his first statement. He turned to Umar, who repeated his first statement. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I shall judge between you with the judgment of Israfil between Jibril and Mikail. That weighed heavily upon the people, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, has Jibril spoken about this? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they are the first of Allah's creation to speak about it. Mikail took the position of Abu Bakr, and Jibril took the position of Umar. Jibril said to Mikail: Whenever we, the people of heaven, differ, the people of earth differ; let us seek judgment from Israfil. So they sought his judgment, and he judged between them with the reality of decree: its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter, all of it from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And I am judging between you. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, had He willed that He not be disobeyed, would not have created Iblis. So Abu Bakr said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. No one narrated this hadith from Muqatil except Umar; Muhammad ibn Yala was alone in transmitting it."
"2652","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Abu Husayn al-Asadi narrated to us, from al-Qasim who said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you five things? Love of the poor and closeness to them; look to who is below you and do not look to who is above you; maintain kinship even if it turns away; speak the truth even if bitter; and say often: There is no power nor strength except through Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Jarir, nor from Jarir except Abu Usamah; Ahmad ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it. And I think the al-Qasim from whom Abu Husayn narrated this hadith is al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah."
"2653","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Umar al-Lahiqi narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the stray camel. He said: What have you to do with it? It has its water-skin and its sandals; it eats trees and comes to water until its owner comes to it. Then he was asked about the stray sheep, and he said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. And he was asked about the mountain pasture theft, and he said: Its value upon him, and its like, and lashes as punishment. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Hammad."
"2654","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, who said: Ziyad sent wealth to the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), favoring Aishah. The messenger kept apologizing to Umm Salamah, so she said: Is Ziyad apologizing to us? One who was greater in favoring her over us than Ziyad used to favor her: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Qays, nor from Qays except Yahya; al-Wakii was alone in transmitting it."
"2655","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Umm Salamah, or Zaynab, or another of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Maymunah had a sheep that died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Why did you not make use of its hide? She said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we make use of it when it is carrion? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purification of the skin is its tanning. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abbad; Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"2656","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from his brother Sad ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lighten the two rakahs before the dawn prayer, until I would say: Did he recite in them the Mother of the Book? Abu Muawiyah said: Then we went to Sad, and he narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah, from Aishah. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya, from his brother Sad, except Abu Muawiyah."
"2657","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The menstruating woman was permitted to depart when she menstruates. He said: And we heard Ibn Umar say at first: She does not depart; then he said: Let her depart; indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted her to depart."
"2658","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from a man called Hurmuz, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, except like for like, equal for equal; sell wheat for barley as you wish, but deferred payment is not permissible; and sell gold for silver as you wish, but deferred payment is not permissible. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Muslim, from Hurmuz, except Muammal."
"2659","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man asked while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting; a man gave him, then people followed in succession. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever establishes a good practice and those after him follow it, he has a reward and the like of the reward of those who follow it after him, without diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever establishes an evil practice, upon him is its sin and from the sins of those who follow him, without diminishing anything from their sins. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muammal. And Sulayman ibn Harb and others narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, as mawquf. And Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, as Muammal narrated it from Hammad."
"2660","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble: Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim (peace be upon them all). No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Hammad; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"2661","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Verses have been revealed to me the like of which were never revealed to me: the two Muawwidhatayn. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail, from Qays, from Abu Masud, except Abd al-Aziz; Ibn Aishah was alone in transmitting it. And Sufyan and others narrated it from Ismail, from Qays, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani."
"2662","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr who said: Ibn Abbas said: Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"2663","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered a sa of dates for him and spoke to his masters, who reduced his tax. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"2664","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Israil al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar who said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: A man from the Ansar came with two water-camels, hastening to feed them at night. He heard the muadhdhin of Muadh when he established the prayer, so he entered and began the prayer with Muadh, who recited Surah al-Baqarah. As soon as the youth saw that, he turned to his own prayer and left Muadh. Muadh said: I shall surely mention what the Ansari did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Ansari came to the Prophet of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, I entered with Muadh in the Maghrib prayer, and he began with Surah al-Baqarah, so I turned to my own prayer and left Muadh. When Muadh entered, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Muadh, are you a trial-maker, are you a trial-maker? Recite By the sun and its brightness, By the night when it covers, and the like. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qays except Wahb."
"2665","And with the same chain, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah who said: The Jews killed a man from the Ansar at Khaybar. His relatives, a people called al-Aharisah, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When they reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the people spoke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eldest, the eldest. He said: Fifty of you must testify. They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we testify to what we did not see, or accept the oaths of the Jews? Camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood-money from his own side with one hundred camels. He said: I saw them, and a she-camel from them kicked me. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Qays except Wahb."
"2666","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Umar al-Muaddib narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Hamdani narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge is only attained by learning, and forbearance only by practicing forbearance; whoever seeks good is given it, and whoever guards against evil is protected from it. Three qualities: whoever has them will not dwell in the highest ranks - and I do not say to you Paradise - whoever practices soothsaying, or seeks divination, or is turned back from a journey by omens. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan."
"2667","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man must not judge between two men while angry. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Hammad, nor from Hammad except Muammal; al-Wakii was alone in transmitting it."
"2668","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith ibn Ghassan al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Corner and the Maqam will come on the Day of Resurrection with a tongue and two lips greater than Abu Qubays, bearing witness for whoever fulfilled them with faithfulness. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Harith ibn Ghassan."
"2669","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining under a tree with his hand under his head. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah against these people whom we fear may turn us back from our religion? He turned his face away from me. I moved to him, and he turned his face away from me three times; each time I said it to him, he turned his face away from me. He sat up on the third time and said: O people, fear Allah; by Allah, a believing man before you would have a saw placed upon his head and be split in two, yet he would not apostatize from his religion. Fear Allah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will grant you victory and act for you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah except Salamah, nor narrated it from Salamah except his two sons Muhammad and Yahya, nor narrated it from Muhammad ibn Salamah except Hassan."
"2670","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Negus died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek forgiveness for your brother. Some people said: He commands us to seek forgiveness for him while he died in the land of Abyssinia? Then was revealed: And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was revealed to you. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Muammal."
"2671","And with the same chain, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood in prayer, would turn to them with his face and say: Straighten yourselves, twice; indeed I see you behind me as I see you before me. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Thabit, except Muammal."
"2672","And with the same chain, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib and Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he bathed from janabah, would wash his hands three times before immersing them in water, then take water with his right and pour it upon his left, then wash his private part, then rinse his mouth three times, inhale water three times, wash his face three times, wash his arms three times each, then pour water upon his head one handful at a time; and when he left his bathing place, he washed his feet."
"2673","And with the same chain, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Ata, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, except Muammal."
"2674","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, saying: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, I send ten upon him for it. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf except Hassan; al-Azraq ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"2675","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Awbad ibn Abi Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, that Aishah said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, one facing my door and the other distant from my door though closer in neighborhood; with which shall I begin? He said: The one facing your door. No one narrated this hadith from Awbad except Bakr."
"2676","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from al-Masudi, from Abd al-Khaliq, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from al-Qarthaa al-Dabbi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me, I saw him persist in four rakahs before Zhuhr. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you persist in four before Zhuhr. He said: It is an hour in which the doors of heaven are opened, and none of them is closed until Zhuhr is prayed; so I love that good be raised for me in that hour. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Khaliq except al-Masudi, nor from al-Masudi except Abbad; Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"2677","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, saying: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Miskin, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fingers will surely be scrutinized for purification, or the Fire will surely seize them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Awanah except Shayban."
"2678","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Sawadah Abu al-Sabbah al-Nakhai narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Zadha who said: Ibn Abbas fell ill with a heavy illness, so he gathered his sons and household to him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs Hajj from Makkah on foot until he returns to it, he has for every step seven hundred good deeds of the good deeds of the Sanctuary. A man said: And what are the good deeds of the Sanctuary, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Every good deed of them is a thousand good deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Isa."
"2679","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Bazi Abu al-Khalil narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin and regrets it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgives him that sin before he seeks forgiveness for it; and whomever Allah bestows a blessing upon and he knows it is from Allah, Allah writes for him its gratitude before he praises Him for it; and whomever Allah clothes with a garment and he knows that Allah is the One who clothed him, the garment does not reach his knees before he is forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Bazi."
"2680","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Sad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from Bayan and Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad al-Fazari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous will depart, one after another, until none remains except dregs like the dregs of dates, whom Allah does not care for. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail, from Bayan, except Ismail ibn Mujalid."
"2681","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab Abu al-Husayn al-Ukli narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Abbad, from his father Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Zayd."
"2682","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yusuf al-Zimmi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not listen to a prophet as He listens to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Quran. And he heard the recitation of Abu Musa and said: This one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq except Ubaydullah."
"2683","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions; when he finished his prayer he turned to the people and said: Do you recite while the imam is reciting? They fell silent. Then he said it three times. Some speakers said: We do. He said: Then do not do so; let each of you recite the Opening of the Book to himself. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ubaydullah."
"2684","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yusuf al-Zimmi narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd al-Kindi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man confesses to adultery four times, and stoning is ordered for him, then he flees, he is left alone. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salamah except Humayd; Abu Bakr was alone in transmitting it."
"2685","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham of usury is greater with Allah than thirty-six acts of adultery. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Ubaydullah."
"2686","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid except Wuhayb."
"2687","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid ibn Uqbah ibn Nizar al-Absi narrated to us, from Hudhayfah ibn Abi Hudhayfah al-Azdi, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi who said: I poured water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in residence and travel; he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, for stool and urine, except for sleep and except for janabah. No one narrated this hadith from Hudhayfah ibn Abi Hudhayfah except al-Walid; Zayd was alone in transmitting it."
"2688","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit who said: I said to Abu Dharr: What interrupts prayer when there is not before you the like of the rear of a saddle? He said: The woman, the donkey, and the black dog. I said: What is the matter with the black dog as distinct from the white or the red? He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: Indeed the black one is a devil, three times. No one narrated it from Hisham al-Dastuwai except Azhar; Ahmad ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"2689","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Amrah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered my house and said: Why do I not see blessing in your house? I said: And what blessing of my house have you found missing? He said: I do not see a sheep in it. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf except Abu Muawiyah; Ahmad ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"2690","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Salim al-Barrad who said: I asked Uqbah ibn Amr about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stood to the mosque, said takbir, then bowed placing his hands upon his knees with his fingers below that, spreading his elbows. He bowed until everything of him settled, then stood until everything of him settled, then prostrated placing his hands upon the ground, spreading his elbows, and prostrated until everything of him settled, then sat until everything of him settled, then prostrated, until he prayed four rakahs. Then he said: Thus I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray. No one narrated this hadith from Mufaddal except Yahya."
"2691","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no envy except in two: a man whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, taught the Quran, so he stands with it during hours of the night and hours of the day; and a man whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave wealth, so he spends it in the path of Allah during hours of the night and hours of the day. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari and Yazid ibn Iyad. Ismail ibn Ayyash was alone in transmitting it from Yahya, and Shayban from Yazid."
"2692","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in a dream that they took the pillar of the Book and carried it to Syria; so when tribulation falls, safety is in Syria. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Muhammad ibn Thawr; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"2693","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from his father who said: Abdullah ibn Masud used to teach a man the tashahhud. Abdullah said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. The man said: Alone, with no partner. Abdullah said: It is thus, but we stop at what we were taught. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib except Mufaddal; Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"2694","And with the same chain, Mufaddal narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from Bilal, that he saw a man praying without completing bowing or prostration, and said: Had this one died, he would have died upon other than the religion of Isa (peace be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mufaddal except Yahya."
"2695","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek trustworthiness - or he said: Look for it - in Quraysh; for the trustworthy one of Quraysh has two merits over the trustworthy of others, and the strong one of Quraysh has two merits over the strong of others."
"2696","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Madini narrated to me, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has no wealth to give in charity, let him seek forgiveness for the believing men and women, for it is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Muhammad; Bakr was alone in transmitting it."
"2697","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The night prayer is two by two; when one of you fears dawn, one rakah makes his prayer odd. No one narrated this hadith from Zaidah except Husayn."
"2698","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd, from a man called Habib, from a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think Ammar ibn Yasir, who said: I spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a need; I spoke to him with yellowness upon my hands. He said to me: Go and wash it off you, three times. So I went with a towel and kept wiping with it the traces of khaluq from between my nails, washing it until it was gone. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: Ask your need. So I conveyed it to him. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Muammal; Ahmad ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"2699","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muammal narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you and you narrate to us, our hearts soften; but when we leave you and see women and do this and that, we find our hearts changed in that hour. He said: Had you remained upon what you are upon with me, the angels would shake hands with you. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"2700","And with the same chain, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas - Hammad said: And I know it only as raised - who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, let each of you walk at his ease; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"2701","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: People asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they pressed him with questions. He ascended the pulpit and said: You do not ask me about anything except that I clarify it for you. I kept looking right and left, seeing every man wrapping his head in his garment, weeping. A man arose who, when he quarreled with men, was attributed to other than his father. He said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Umar stood and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet; we seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah, the anger of His Messenger, and the evil of tribulations. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have never seen the like of today in good and evil; Paradise and Hellfire were depicted to me until I saw them below the wall. Qatadah used to mention at this hadith this verse: O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if made manifest to you, would distress you. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Azhar; Ahmad ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"2702","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, saying: Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: I often saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the prayer while donkeys crowded before him."
"2703","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani narrated to us, saying: Al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He stood for prayer, stood long, then bowed long, then prostrated, then repeated the like. Ikrimah said: Ibn Abbas said: I was beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not hear the recitation."
"2704","And from Ibn Abbas who said: A spear was planted before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat while he prayed, and donkeys passed beyond the spear."
"2705","And from Ikrimah who said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the hour in Friday upon the pulpit, minimizing it with his finger. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Hakam ibn Aban except Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani."
"2706","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Kaysan, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The names of the two angels who come in the grave are Munkar and Nakir; and the names of Harut and Marut while they were in heaven were Azra and Uzayr. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Kaysan except Isa; Yaqub was alone in transmitting it."
"2707","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, saying: Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali who said: My father narrated to me from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a community from the communities, forty men or more, bear witness, Allah permits their testimony. No one narrated this hadith from Salih except Sawadah; Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj was alone in transmitting it."
"2708","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil, from Mansur, from Mujahid, who said: I entered the mosque with Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn Umar was leaning against the chamber of Aishah, with people praying Duha. Urwah said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is this prayer? He said: An innovation. Urwah said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how many Umrahs did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform? He said to him: Four, one of them in Rajab. We heard Aishah clearing her throat in the chamber. He said to her: Abu Abd al-Rahman claims that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed four Umrahs, one of them in Rajab. She said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never performed Umrah except while he was with him, and he never performed Umrah in Rajab at all."
"2709","And with the same chain: From Mujahid, from Yusuf who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he granted inheritance to the son of the slave-woman of Zamah, because he was born upon the bed of Zamah, and said to Sawdah: As for you, veil yourself from him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Mufaddal except Yahya."
"2710","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib and Musa ibn Abi Jafar al-Farra, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin from Banu Sad ibn Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you, O lad of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: And upon you peace. He said: I am a man from your maternal uncles, from Banu Sad ibn Bakr; I am the messenger of my people to you and their delegate. I shall question you, and my questioning of you will be severe, and I shall adjure you, and my adjuring of you will be severe. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Ask, O brother of Banu Sad ibn Bakr. He said: Who created you, created those before you, and who is created after you? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that: Did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths, and caused provision to flow between them? He said: Allah. He said: I adjure you by that: Did He send you? He said: Yes. He said: We found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to pray by night and day five prayers at their times; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to fast the month of Ramadan; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: We found in your Book and your messengers commanded us to take from the edges of our wealth and place it among our poor; I adjure you by that: Did He command you? He said: Yes. He said: Then he said: As for the fifth, I shall not ask about it, nor do I have need of it - meaning indecencies. Then he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall act upon them, and whoever of my people obeys me. Then he turned back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, then said: If he speaks the truth, he will enter Paradise thereby."
"2711","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things I shall not abandon: sleeping upon witr, the Duha prayer, and fasting three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Zurah except Jarir."
"2712","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Nadr Abu Umar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not speak obscenely; and I forbade you from the meat of sacrifices after three days, so eat and keep; and I forbade you to drink from gourds, green jars, pitch-coated vessels, and hollowed stumps, so drink, but do not drink intoxicants. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the intoxicant? He said: Drink it, O Umar; when you fear it, leave it."
"2713","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has added a prayer for you, and it is the witr. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Nadr al-Khazzaz except Abu Yahya."
"2714","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that he prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a woman behind him, until people came later. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ismail."
"2715","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr al-Fuqaymi, from Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The hypocrites today are worse than the hypocrites who were in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because those concealed it while these proclaim it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, except Muhammad ibn Fudayl. And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah."
"2716","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Abu Kudaynah Yahya ibn al-Muhallab, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Hibbal ibn Rufaydah, from Masruq, that he entered upon Aishah on the day doubted of Ramadan. She said: O slave-girl, prepare sawiq for him. He said: I am fasting. She said: Have you preceded the month? I said: No, but I fasted all of Shaban, and that coincided with this day. She said: Some people used to precede the month, fasting before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: O you who believe, do not advance before Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Kudaynah except Abu Usamah."
"2717","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Aishah narrated to us, saying: Juwayriyah ibn Asma narrated to us, saying: Al-Saaq ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Farazdaq who said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: I see you small of feet; if you can have for them tomorrow a place at the Hawd, do so. I said: And what is that? He said: I heard him say - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed I have a Hawd to which my community will come, as between Sanaa and Yathrib. This hadith is not narrated from al-Farazdaq except with this chain."
"2718","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Hammad, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I leave you; those before you were destroyed only by their differing over their prophets. When I command you with something, come to it; and when I forbid you something, avoid it as much as you can. No one narrated it from Ayyub except Hammad, nor narrated it from Hammad except Ali."
"2719","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, saying: Misar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named himself names for us, among them what we remembered. He said: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffi, and the Prophet of mercy, and the Prophet of battle. No one narrated it from Misar except Jafar, nor narrated it from Jafar except al-Wakii."
"2720","Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man from the Ansar. When he drew near his dwelling he heard him speaking inside. When he sought permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I heard you speaking to another. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I had entered into grief over people's talk because of my fever, when one entered upon me - I have never seen after you a man more noble in assembly nor better in speech than him. He said: That was Jibril (peace be upon him); and among you are men such that if one of them swears by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He fulfills it. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain, and none narrated it except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab."
"2721","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, saying: Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, who said: I taught Ibn Sirin the tashahhud; I narrated to him from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he took my tashahhud and left his own. No one narrated it from Shubah except Umayyah, nor narrated it from Umayyah except Umayyah and Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan."
"2722","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Fadl Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Khattab ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakrah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would order the killing of every pitch-black one; so kill the helper ones among dogs, for they are the accursed among the jinn. No one narrated it from Umarah except Abd al-Malik; Abdullah ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"2723","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not seek the merit of fasting one day over another after Ramadan, except the day of Ashura. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Said, nor narrated it from Said except Muhammad ibn Sawa; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."
"2724","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Amr ibn Dinar who said: Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I have not seen better than Fatimah except her father. She said: There was something between them, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, ask her, for she does not lie."
"2725","And from Rawh, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, that two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the Farewell Hajj asking him for charity. He raised his gaze to them and lowered it, seeing them as two sturdy men. He said: If you wish, I shall help you with it; but there is no share in it for a rich one, nor for a strong earner."
"2726","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Habib ibn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Ibn Umm Maktum over Madinah to lead the people in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Habib; Yazid was alone in transmitting it."
"2727","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah narrated to us, saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrate from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offering him a camel of mine, and I saw him pray Duha six rakahs. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Mutamir was alone in transmitting it."
"2728","And with the same chain he said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrate from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted kissing and cupping for the fasting one. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Mutamir."
"2729","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise, and he said: Do not torment your children by pressing the throat for udhrah. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Abd al-Wahhab."
"2730","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah narrated to us, saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrate from Muhammad ibn Qays, that Umm Hani narrated that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her at the time of the Conquest and prayed Duha six rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Mutamir."
"2731","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr who said: I said to Ali ibn Husayn: I testify regarding Abd Khayr that he narrated to me that he heard Ali say upon this pulpit: The best of this community after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar; and he said: Had I wished, I would name a third. Ali ibn Husayn struck his hand upon my thigh and said: Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Husayn except Hakim ibn Jubayr."
"2732","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Umayyah narrated to us, saying: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah narrate from Abdullah ibn Wahb, that Uthman said to Ibn Umar: Go and be a judge. He said: Will you excuse me, O Commander of the Faithful? For I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is a judge and judges in ignorance is of the people of the Fire; and whoever is a knowledgeable judge and judges with truth or justice, he asks to escape even. So what do I hope from it after this? This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Mutamir was alone in transmitting it."
"2733","And with the same chain he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah narrate from Abu Bakr ibn Bashir, from Kab ibn Ujrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Kab ibn Ujrah, when rulers are over you, whoever enters upon them, believes their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing, is not of me nor am I of him, and will not come to me at the Hawd; and whoever enters upon them and does not believe their lies nor aid them in their wrongdoing, is of me and I am of him. O Kab ibn Ujrah, no flesh nor blood grown from unlawful earnings enters Paradise; every flesh and blood grown from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of it. O Kab ibn Ujrah, people go out in the morning and return: one going out to ransom his neck, thus freeing it; and one going out, thus destroying it. O Kab, prayer is a proof, fasting is a shield, and charity removes sin as ice melts upon a smooth rock. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Bashir except Abd al-Malik; Mutamir was alone in transmitting it."
"2734","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, saying: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any boy who performs Hajj then reaches maturity must perform another Hajj; any Bedouin who performs Hajj then migrates must perform another Hajj; and any slave who performs Hajj then is freed must perform another Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah in marfu form except Yazid; Muhammad ibn al-Minhal was alone in transmitting it."
"2735","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, saying: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jaad, from Jabir who said: We were one thousand four hundred - meaning the day water became scarce - so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel of water, placed his palm in it, and water gushed from between his fingers. They washed, performed ablution, and drank. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Qays."
"2736","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four before Zhuhr are like their equal after Isha, and four after Isha are like their equal of Laylat al-Qadr. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Yahya."
"2737","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, saying: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, cursed wine itself, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its pourer, its drinker, and the eater of its price. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Yaqub."
"2738","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it; for in one wing is poison and in the other is cure. No one narrated this hadith from Abbad except Amr."
"2739","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, saying: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I take a sheep to slaughter it and I pity it. He said: And the sheep: if you pity it, Allah will pity you. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Adi; Ali ibn al-Jaad was alone in transmitting it."
"2740","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, saying: Rayhan ibn Said narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will support this religion with people who have no share in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abbad and Mamar ibn Rashid. Rayhan was alone in transmitting it from Abbad, and Rabah ibn Zayd from Mamar."
"2741","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever does not inherit from the Muslim, nor the Muslim from the disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Husayn."
"2742","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman gives charity from her husband's wealth without spoiling, she has her reward, her husband has the reward of what he earned, and the storekeeper likewise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, except Jarir. And Sufyan al-Thawri and others narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Aishah."
"2743","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, saying: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has changed in color. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, except Mubarak."
"2744","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Jaad narrated to us, saying: Bahr ibn Kunayz al-Saqqa narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animal for animal, two for one on credit, and saw no harm in it hand to hand."
"2745","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the boy has not eaten food, water is poured over his urine; and when it is a girl, she is washed thoroughly. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan, from his mother, except Ismail; Abd al-Rahim was alone in transmitting it."
"2746","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ammar ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When allegiance is given to two caliphs, kill the latter of them. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Hilal."
"2747","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us, saying: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited talbiyah, would say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise, blessing, and dominion are Yours; there is no partner for You. No one narrated this hadith from Salih except Said."
"2748","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us from Umar, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah who said: We used to prepare nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin tied at the top with a hanging strap; we prepared it in the morning and he drank it in the evening, and prepared it in the evening and he drank it in the morning. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Abd al-Wahhab."
"2749","Ibrahim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr while in a tent: O Allah, I ask You Your covenant and Your promise; O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today. Abu Bakr took his hand and said: Enough, O Messenger of Allah; you have pressed your Lord. He was in armor, bringing out his hand, saying: The multitude will be defeated and turn their backs; rather the Hour is their appointment, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid except Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi."
"2750","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, from Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever prays four rakahs before Zhuhr, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbids his flesh to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Yazid; Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"2751","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam upon his wall. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, except Yazid; Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"2752","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And We removed whatever rancor was in their breasts. He said: When the believers are delivered from reckoning, they are held at a bridge between the Fire and Paradise, and settle wrongs that were between them in this world. When they are purified, they are ordered to enter Paradise. By Allah, they know their dwellings in Paradise better than they knew their dwellings in this world. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah with this wording except Said ibn Abi Arubah; Yazid was alone in transmitting it."
"2753","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Awn narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: Eating the meat of domestic donkeys was forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Ismail."
"2754","Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Said al-Abahh narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: We used to recognize the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he approached us by the fragrance of his scent."
"2755","And from Anas who said: I never touched silk brocade, nor silk, nor anything softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2756","2753 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abdillah ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a boy or a girl and said: ""If anyone were to be saved from the squeezing of the grave, this boy would have been saved."" No one narrated this hadith from Thumamah except Hammad."
"2757","2754 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept chanting the talbiyah until he stoned the jamrah. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Abd al-Warith."
"2758","2755 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna al-Attar al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz - meaning Abu Sukayn - narrated to me, he said: I came to Anas ibn Malik and said: Inform me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he led us in the Zhuhr prayer, and recited in a soft recitation al-Mursalat, al-Nazi'at, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and similar surahs. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Sukayn except al-Muthanna al-Attar; Sukayn alone narrated it."
"2759","2756 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abdillah ibn Abi Utbah, the freedman of Anas, from Anas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked something, that would be seen in his face. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh alone narrated it."
"2760","2757 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he hastened in the valley, said: ""O Allah, forgive and have mercy, and You are the Mightiest, the Most Generous."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Layth; Abd al-Warith alone narrated it."
"2761","2758 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: On the day of Hunayn the people fled from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that it be announced: ""O companions of Surat al-Baqarah, O company of the Ansar!"" Then the call intensified among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. When they heard the call they came forward; by Allah, I likened them only to camels yearning for their young. When they met, fighting became fierce, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Now the oven has heated up."" And he took a handful of pebbles and threw them, and said: ""They are defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah."" And Ali ibn Abi Talib was among the fiercest of people in fighting that day. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, except Imran; Amr alone narrated it."
"2762","2759 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Abdillah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from his father, from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who steps with his sandals in filth. He said: ""Dust is purification for them."" No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Yazid."
"2763","2760 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abu Ishaq, from his father, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Ma'mar, and no one from Ma'mar except Yazid; Muhammad alone narrated it."
"2764","2761 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Shuqran who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a donkey, facing toward Khaybar. This hadith is not narrated from Shuqran except with this chain; Muslim alone narrated it."
"2765","2762 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, that he heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The example of the sinner among the people is like the example of a people who boarded a ship at sea and divided it among themselves, so each one of them got a place. Then one of them set out to make a hole in his place. They said: Do you want to drown us? He said: What business is it of yours with my place? If they leave him, they will drown and he will drown with them, and if they seize his hand, they will be saved and he will be saved. That is the example of the sinner."" No one narrated this hadith from Salamah except his son Muhammad, and no one from Muhammad except Hassan; al-Azraq alone narrated it."
"2766","2763 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hawtharah ibn Ashras al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If a man invited people to a fleshy bone or two trotters, they would respond to him, yet they are invited to this congregational prayer and do not come to it. I have indeed intended to order a man to lead the people in congregational prayer, then turn to a people who heard the call and did not respond, and set it ablaze over them with fire. And none stays away from it except a hypocrite."" No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"2767","2764 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Tahir narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Dharr who said: I had a brother called Unays who was a poet. He and another poet challenged each other to a contest. Unays said: I am more poetic than you, and the other said: I am more poetic. Unays said: Whom do you accept to judge between us? He said: I accept the soothsayer of Makkah to be between us. He said: Yes. So they went out to Makkah and met at the soothsayer; each recited his words to him, and he said to Unays: I have judged in your favor - as if he preferred the poetry of Unays. Then he said: O my brother, in Makkah there is a man who claims to be a prophet, and he follows your religion. Ibn Abbas said: I said to Abu Dharr: And what was your religion? He said: I had turned away from the gods of my people which they worshipped. I said: What did you worship? He said: Nothing. I used to pray at night until I would fall down as if I were a mere shadow, until the heat of the sun would wake me. I said: Where did you face? He said: Wherever my Lord directed me. Then Unays said to me - and they had grown weary of him, meaning they disliked him. Abu Dharr said: So I came until I entered Makkah, and I stayed between the Ka'bah and its curtains for fifteen nights and days. Every night I would go out and drink a draught from Zamzam water, and I felt no pangs of hunger in my liver, though my belly became wrinkled. Two women were invoking their gods one night; one of them said: O Isaf, grant me a boy, and the other said: O Na'ilah, grant me such-and-such. So I said: Vulva for vulva. They turned away saying: The Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its curtains. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by with Abu Bakr walking behind him, and they said: The Sabian is between the Ka'bah and its curtains. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke words condemning what they had said. Abu Dharr said: I thought he was the Messenger of Allah, so I went out to him and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah,"" three times. Then he said to me: ""How long have you been here?"" I said: For fifteen days and nights. He said: ""From where did you eat?"" He said: Every night at midnight I would come to Zamzam and drink a draught from it, and I felt no pangs of hunger in my liver, though my belly became wrinkled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is food and drink, and it is blessed."" He said it three times. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me: ""From whom are you?"" I said: From Ghifar. Ghifar used to waylay the pilgrims, and it was as if the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew from me. He said to Abu Bakr: ""Let us go, O Abu Bakr."" So we went to the house of Abu Bakr, and he brought us raisins and we ate from them. I stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he taught me Islam, and I recited something of the Quran. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to proclaim my religion openly. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I fear for you that you will be killed."" I said: It must be. He said: ""I fear for you that you will be killed."" I said: It must be, O Messenger of Allah, even if I am killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent toward me. Quraysh were sitting in circles talking in the mosque, and I said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. The circles broke up and they rose against me and beat me until they left me like a red idol, and they thought they had killed me. I got up and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he saw my condition and said to me: ""Did I not forbid you?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, it was a need in myself, so I fulfilled it. I stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: ""Join your people, and when you hear of my triumph, come to me."" So I came, having stayed away from them a long time. I met Unays; he wept and said: O my brother, I thought you had been killed when you stayed away from us so long. What did you do? Did you meet the companion you sought? I said: Yes. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Unays said: O my brother, I have no aversion to you; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. And he became Muslim on the spot. Then I came to my mother; when she saw me she wept and said: O my son, you stayed away from us until I feared you had been killed. What did you do? Did you meet the companion you sought? I said: Yes. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. She said: What did Unays do? I said: He became Muslim. She said: I have no aversion to you two; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So I stayed among my people, and many of them became Muslim, until we heard of the triumph of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I came to him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yazid al-Madini except Abu Tahir, the freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali; Ja'far ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"2768","2765 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Muzarrid, from Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Talhah who said: I entered the mosque and recognized hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I asked Umm Sulaym: Do you have anything? She gestured with her hands and said: I have something. I said: Prepare it, knead, and I sent Anas saying: Go and whisper in his ear and invite him. When Anas came forward, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is a man who has come to you bringing you something. Did Abu Talhah send you to invite us?"" Anas said: Yes. He said: ""Rise, in the name of Allah."" Anas turned away hurrying until he came to Abu Talhah and said: This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming to you with the people. Abu Talhah said: So I met him at the door at the resting place of the stairs and said: What have you done to us, O Messenger of Allah? I only recognized hunger in your face, so I prepared something for you to eat. He said: ""Enter and rejoice."" So he entered, and her tray was brought. He began smoothing it with his hand, then said: ""Is there any?"" - as if meaning condiment. So we brought him our skin containing something, or containing nothing. He took it in his hand, and ghee poured out of it. He said: ""Admit ten by ten to me."" He said: And they were about a hundred. They entered and ate until they were full, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them about the leftover that remained: ""Eat, you and your families."" So they ate and were full. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah except Mu'awiyah; Hatim alone narrated it."
"2769","2766 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard an ugly name, he changed it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani al-Wasiti except al-Salt ibn Mas'ud."
"2770","2767 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever I am mentioned before, let him send blessings upon me, for whoever sends blessings upon me once, ten blessings will be sent upon him."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Ibrahim."
"2771","2768 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from his mother, from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, that she heard her father al-Husayn ibn Ali saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""There is no Muslim man or woman afflicted with a calamity who then remembers it, even long after its time, and renews the istirja' for it, except that Allah renews for him at that moment and Allah gives him the reward thereof on the day he was afflicted with it."" This hadith is not narrated from al-Husayn ibn Ali except with this chain; Hisham Abu al-Miqdam alone narrated it."
"2772","2769 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As al-Thaqafi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The gates of heaven are opened at midnight, and a caller calls: Is there any supplicant so that he may be answered? Is there any asker so that he may be given? Is there any distressed one so that he may be relieved? So no Muslim remains who supplicates with a supplication except that Allah Almighty answers him, except an adulteress who traffics with her private part, or a tax-collector."" No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Dawud; Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"2773","2770 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrating from A'ishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Do not say of your dead except good."" No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah except al-Furat."
"2774","2771 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that two women came to Dawud (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the wolf had eaten the son of one of them - disputing over the remaining one. Dawud judged in favor of the elder. When they went out to Sulayman, he said: How did he judge between you? They informed him. He said: Bring me the knife. Abu Hurayrah said: The first one I heard saying ""the knife"" from, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is myself; we used to call it al-mudyah. The younger said: Why? He said: So that I may cut him between you. She said: Give him to her. So Sulayman judged in favor of the younger, and said: If he were your son, you would not agree to cut him."
"2775","2772 - And from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from Abu Ayyub, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a dog."" Thus Rawh narrated this hadith, saying: from Abu Ayyub. And all the people narrated it from Suhayl, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from Abu Talhah."
"2776","2773 - And from Rawh, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the road to Makkah and passed by a mountain called Jumdan. He said: ""This is Jumdan. Proceed. The mufarridun have preceded"" - twice. They said: And who are the mufarridun, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Those men and women who remember Allah much. May Allah have mercy on those who shave."" They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave."" They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""May Allah have mercy on those who shave."" They said: And those who shorten, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""And those who shorten."""
"2777","2774 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hasten with deeds before tribulations like patches of the dark night: a man wakes up a believer and sleeps as a disbeliever, and sleeps as a believer and wakes up as a disbeliever, selling his religion for a portion of this world."""
"2778","2775 - And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Every good deed the son of Adam does, I reward him for it with ten good deeds up to seven hundredfold, except fasting; it is Mine and I reward for it. He leaves food for My sake and leaves desire for My sake; it is Mine and I reward for it. Fasting is a shield. Whoever is fasting, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly. If a man reviles him or harms him, let him say: I am fasting, I am fasting."""
"2779","2776 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""How will you be, O Abdillah ibn Amr, when you are among the dregs of the people?"" He said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""That is when their trusts and covenants are corrupted and they become like this"" - and he interlaced his fingers. He said: What should I do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Act upon what you recognize and leave what you disapprove, act for your own self, and leave the common people."""
"2780","2777 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The religion began strange, and the religion will return strange as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."""
"2781","2778 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do you know who the bankrupt is?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, the bankrupt among us is one who has no dirham and no goods. He said: ""The bankrupt of my nation is one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with fasting, prayer, and charity, but comes having wronged this one, consumed the wealth of this one, struck this one, and reviled this one. So he is seated, and retribution is exacted for this one from his good deeds and for this one from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before what is owed of sins is settled, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, then he will be thrown into the Fire."""
"2782","2779 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah, no one would hope for His Paradise, and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, no servant would despair of His Paradise. Allah created mercy as a hundred mercies, and sent down one mercy among His servants by which they show mercy to one another, and with Allah are ninety-nine. And this fire is one part of a hundred parts of Hell."""
"2783","2780 - And with the same chain, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""A man may work for a long time with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then Allah seals his work with the deeds of the people of the Fire, and makes him among the people of the Fire. And a man may work for a long time with the deeds of the people of the Fire, then Allah seals his work with the deeds of the people of Paradise, and makes him among the people of Paradise."""
"2784","2781 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and believe in me and in what I have brought. When they do that, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."""
"2785","2782 - And with the same chain, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever."""
"2786","2783 - And with the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will come upon the people a time when a man will call his cousin and his relative: Come to prosperity - while Madinah is better for them, if they only knew."""
"2787","2784 - And with the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not come until Madinah expels its wicked as the bellows expels the dross of iron."""
"2788","2785 - And with the same chain, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool down with the prayer."""
"2789","2786 - And with the same chain, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whom I join ties with while they cut me off, I forbear toward them while they act ignorantly toward me, and I do good to them while they do evil to me. He said: ""If it is as you say, it is as if you feed them hot ashes, and there will remain with you a helper from Allah against them as long as you persist in that."""
"2790","2787 - And from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Bujayr ibn Abi Bujayr, from Abdillah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a hunting dog nor a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."""
"2791","2788 - And from Abdillah ibn Amr, that they were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey, and they passed by the grave of Abu Righal. They said: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""This is the grave of Abu Righal, and he is the father of Thaqif. He was a man of Thamud, and his dwelling was in the Sanctuary. When Allah destroyed his people with what He destroyed them with, his place in the Sanctuary protected him. He went out until, when he reached here, he died and was buried, and with him was buried a branch of gold. So we hastened to it and dug it out."""
"2792","2789 - And with the same chain, from Rawh, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Sayfi, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh to Yemen and said: ""You are coming to a people of the Scripture, so let the first thing you call them to be the worship of Allah. When they recognize Allah, inform them that Allah Almighty has obligated upon them prayers in their day and night. When they do that, inform them that Allah Almighty has obligated upon them the zakah of their wealth."""
"2793","2790 - And from Rawh, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, that Abu Basrah Humayl ibn Basrah met Abu Hurayrah while he was returning from al-Tur, and said: Had I met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The livers of riding camels are saddled only toward three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa."""
"2794","2791 - And from Rawh, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that he heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Allah Almighty will not look at one who drags his garment out of arrogance on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2795","2792 - And from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him not leave anyone to pass in front of him; if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is a devil."""
"2796","2793 - And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar, that he carried a horse in the path of Allah, then found it with its owner who had neglected it, and he was of little wealth and wanted to buy it. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: ""Do not buy it, even if you are given it for a dirham, for the example of one who takes back his gift is like the example of the dog that returns to its vomit."""
"2797","2794 - And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar, from al-Sunabihi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""When the servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth and nose, his sins exit from his face until they exit from beneath his eyelids. When he washes his hands, his sins exit from his hands until they exit from beneath his nails. When he wipes his head, his sins exit from his head until they exit from between his ears. When he washes his feet, his sins exit from his feet until they exit from beneath his toenails."""
"2798","2795 - And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his mother, from Hafsah bint Umar who said: I heard Umar saying: O Allah, death in Your path, and passing away in the land of Your Prophet. I said: And how can that be? He said: ""Allah will bring it about when He wills."""
"2799","2796 - And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Mu'adh ibn Abdillah ibn Khubayb, from his father who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the road to Makkah, and a mist came upon us and separated the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Where are the people?"" I said: The mist has separated them. He said: ""Say."" I said: What shall I say? He said: ""{Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak}"" until he completed it. So I said it. He said: ""People and creation have never sought refuge with anything like it."""
"2800","2797 - And from Rawh, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When this verse was revealed: ""{And those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses},"" Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: If I saw a man with my wife, would I wait until I bring four? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Yes."" He said: No, by the One Who sent you with the truth - if I saw him, I would hasten against him with the sword. He said: ""Look, O company of the Ansar, at what your chief says. Sa'd is indeed jealous, and I am more jealous than him, and Allah Almighty is more jealous than me."""
"2801","2798 - And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah, that Fatimah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for a servant, complaining to him of work. He said: ""I have not found any with us."" Then he said: ""Shall I not guide you to what is better than a servant? Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times when you take your bed."""
"2802","2799 - And with the same chain, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The curse of Allah, the angels, and all people is upon a man who claims the freedmen of a people without the permission of their masters."""
"2803","2800 - And from Rawh, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty loves a servant, He says to Jibril: I love so-and-so. So Jibril loves him, then Jibril calls to the inhabitants of heaven: Allah Almighty loves so-and-so, so love him. So they love him. Then acceptance is placed for him on earth. And evil is likewise."""
"2804","2801 - And from Rawh, from Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: We came to Madinah while a man of Banu Ghifar called Siba' ibn Urfutah had been appointed over Madinah. We prayed the dawn prayer with him; he recited in the first rak'ah Surah Maryam, and in the other ""{Woe to those who give short measure}."" Among us was a man who gave short measure. When we finished the prayer, we said: Woe to so-and-so. Then we came to him and caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had conquered Khaybar. The people gave permission for him to allot us a share of the spoils, so he gave permission to him, and he allotted to us."
"2805","2802 - And from Rawh, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that a man place one of his feet over the other in prayer."
"2806","2803 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr Abu Abbad al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn Abi Umarah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended, so when one of you enters them, let him say: In the name of Allah. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils, and from the accursed Satan."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except Adi; Qatan alone narrated it."
"2807","2804 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking truth when he sees it, or reminding of a grave matter, for speaking truth or reminding of a grave matter neither brings an end near nor distances a provision."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Mu'alla except Ja'far."
"2808","2805 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the sun eclipses, pray as the least prayer you have prayed."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh alone narrated it."
"2809","2806 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Uthman al-Ghatafani narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Barzah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleeping before the last Isha and talking after it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah except Khalid; Uthman alone narrated it."
"2810","2807 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Musayyab Abu Raja' al-Kalbi narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The women came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken the merit and jihad, so command us to a deed by which we may attain the merit of jihad in the path of Allah. He said: ""The occupation of one of you in her house attains thereby the deed of the mujahid in the path of Allah."" No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Rawh."
"2811","2808 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Awbad ibn Abi Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Anas, perform ablution well, your life will be lengthened; greet whomever you meet of my nation, your good deeds will multiply; when you enter your house, greet, the good of your house will multiply; have mercy on the young and honor the elder."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Imran except his son Awbad."
"2812","2809 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and forbade jallalah animals - riding them and eating their meat - and forbade that a woman be married together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."
"2813","2810 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The people of camels and the people of sheep boasted before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Pride and arrogance are among the people of camels, and tranquility and dignity are among the people of sheep."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"2814","2811 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating, and I know him only from Nafi' ibn Abd al-Harith, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden of the gardens of Madinah and sat on the edge of the well. Abu Bakr came asking permission, and he said: ""Permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" Then Umar came asking permission, and he said: ""Permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" Then Uthman entered asking permission, and he said: ""Permit him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise along with a trial."" No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Abd al-Aziz."
"2815","2812 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Abdillah al-Danaj narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me, he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and he would say takbir when he lowered and when he raised. I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: It is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah al-Danaj except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"2816","2813 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Umar al-Abdi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Jibril (peace be upon him) and extended his hand to him, but he refused to take it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and performed ablution, then extended his hand to him, and he took it. He said: O Jibril, what prevented you from taking my hand? He said: You had taken the hand of a Jew, so I disliked that my hand touch a hand touched by the hand of a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Umar; Sa'id alone narrated it."
"2817","2814 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, and Maymun ibn Siyah and Ja'far ibn Zayd, from Anas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah, so beware lest Allah hold you to account for anything of His protection."" No one narrated this hadith from Salih except Sa'id."
"2818","2815 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Yahya Abu Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: ""I shall surely send a man whom Allah will not disgrace."" So he sent for Ali while he was in the baggage grinding, and none of you would grind. They brought him with inflamed eyes. He said: O Prophet of Allah, I can hardly see. So he spat in his eyes, shook the banner three times, then handed it to him, and victory was granted to him, and he brought Safiyyah bint Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins: ""Which of you will befriend me in this world and the Hereafter?"" He said to each man of them: ""O so-and-so, will you befriend me in this world and the Hereafter?"" - three times - and he would say: No; until he passed the last of them. Ali said: O Prophet of Allah, I am your ally in this world and the Hereafter. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You are my ally in this world and the Hereafter."" He said: And he sent Abu Bakr with Surat al-Tawbah, and sent Ali after him. Abu Bakr said: O Ali, perhaps Allah and His Messenger are displeased with me. Ali said: No, but the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not fitting that any but a man from me - and I from him - should convey from me."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his garment over Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, then said: ""{Allah only wishes to remove defilement from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}."" And he was the first to become Muslim after Khadijah among the people. He said: And Ali risked himself; he wore the garment of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then slept in his place. He said: And the polytheists were pelting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2819","2816 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran informed us, he said: Abu Imran Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather - and he had companionship - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a group approaching and said: ""The Azd have come to you, the best of people in faces, the sweetest in mouths, the most truthful in meeting."" And he looked at a dense crowd approaching and said: ""Who are these?"" They said: These are Bakr ibn Wa'il. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, mend their broken, shelter their outcast, and do not show me a beggar among them."" This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah except with this chain; al-Shadhakuni alone narrated it."
"2820","2817 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Muti' ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever endears himself to people with what they love, while openly opposing Allah with what they hate, will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him."" This hadith is not narrated except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"2821","2818 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: I heard Abu Bakr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Disbelief in Allah is claiming a lineage that is not known, and disbelief in Allah is disowning a lineage, even if slight."" No one narrated this hadith from Bayan except al-Sari."
"2822","2819 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah ibn Sa'id al-Aslami narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman, from his father, from Uthman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""One strike with a whip suffices you against the snake, whether you hit it or miss it."" This hadith is not narrated from Uthman except with this chain; al-Shadhakuni alone narrated it."
"2823","2820 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir who said: Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi narrated to me, he said: I bear witness concerning Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he bore witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Bathing on Friday is obligatory for every adult, and that he use the toothstick, and touch perfume."" No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Harami ibn Umarah."
"2824","2821 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped in Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Yusuf."
"2825","2822 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in stagnant water."" No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Farwah except Abd al-Salam; Sulayman alone narrated it."
"2826","2823 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh and limas. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Warith."
"2827","2824 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah, the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should pray while feeling any discomfort - meaning stool and urine."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except his nephew; al-Waqidi alone narrated it."
"2828","2825 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid, the nephew of Hazm al-Quta'i, narrated to us, he said: al-Khasib ibn Jahdar narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Jahdar, from Ubaydillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor memory. He said: ""Seek help with your right hand."" This hadith is not narrated from Ubaydillah ibn Abi Bakr except with this chain; Isma'il alone narrated it."
"2829","2826 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid, the nephew of Hazm, narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Anas who said: A'ishah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, with which of them should I begin? He said: ""With the one whose door is nearer to you."" No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except the nephew of Hazm; Isma'il alone narrated it."
"2830","2827 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar and Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara' ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man, when he takes his bed, to say: ""O Allah, I have turned my face to You, entrusted my back to You, in fear and hope of You. There is no refuge nor escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Prophet whom You sent."" No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar and Habib except Hammad."
"2831","2828 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abu Ma'shar, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves three Fridays without excuse, his heart will be sealed."" No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abu Ma'shar; Hassan alone narrated it. And the people narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ubaydah ibn Sufyan, from Abu al-Ja'd al-Damri."
"2832","2829 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham handed us a book and said: I heard it from my father. In it was: from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram in his Hajj during one of the two evening prayers. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham, and no one from Hisham except Mu'adh in his book."
"2833","2830 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Khayyat narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Karib, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to the heels from the Fire."" No one narrated this hadith from Umar except Abu Ubaydah."
"2834","2831 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata' al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and Indian costus."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id; Abd al-Wahhab alone narrated it."
"2835","2832 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from al-Mughirah - the son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar - from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken, I came upon the lowest heaven, and there were men whose tongues and lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are the preachers of your nation."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah, the son-in-law of Malik, except Hisham."
"2836","2833 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from A'ishah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O A'ishah, if only we had someone to talk to us, and I would benefit from him. I said: Shall we not send for Abu Bakr? He fell silent. Then he said: ""O A'ishah, if only we had someone to talk to us."" And I seized the opportunity from him. I said: Shall we not send for Umar? He fell silent toward me, and called a servant of his and whispered to him. Then Uthman asked permission, and he permitted him. He leaned over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaned over him, and they kept whispering to each other. By Allah, I do not know what they said. When he raised his head, he turned away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: ""O Uthman, perhaps Allah will clothe you with a shirt; if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off"" - three times. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, where were you regarding this hadith? She said: I forgot it, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, until the man was killed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Zubaydi; Faraj alone narrated it."
"2837","2834 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Sinani narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him, east and west, and would pray witr on it. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except al-Fadl."
"2838","2835 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Abdillah al-Jasri, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty dislikes three things for you: gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran; Ibn Qutaybah alone narrated it."
"2839","2836 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam is created with ninety-nine deaths beside him; if his deaths miss him, he is thrust into old age until he dies."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran; Salm alone narrated it."
"2840","2837 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Harmalah ibn Imran, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith al-Azdi, from Gharafah ibn al-Harith who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj when the camels were brought. He said: ""Call Abu al-Hasan for me."" So Ali was called, and he said: ""Take the lower end of the spear."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took its upper end. When he finished, he rode the mule and seated Ali behind him. This hadith is not narrated from Gharafah except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi alone narrated it."
"2841","2838 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Jariyah ibn Harim al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Busr al-Hubrani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Kabshah al-Anmari narrating from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever deliberately lies about me, or rejects anything I commanded, let him take his seat in the Fire."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Kabshah, from Abu Bakr, except with this chain; Amr ibn Malik alone narrated it."
"2842","2839 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Sarhah al-Tanukhi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn al-As, from Uthman ibn Affan, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in what is the salvation of this nation? He said: ""In the word which I offered to my uncle and he refused: bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."" No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Umar ibn Sa'id."
"2843","2840 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami informed us, he said: Umar, the freedman of the family of Manzur ibn Sayyar, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah al-Umari, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was circumambulating the House, his sandal strap broke. A man untied a strap from his sandal then handed it to him, but he refused to take it and said: ""This is favoritism, and I do not accept favoritism."" No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Umar, the freedman of the family of Sayyar; Umar ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"2844","2841 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Husayn al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, he said: Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyaynah, narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended a journey, he would set out on Thursday. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil except Ibn Ulathah; Amr ibn al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"2845","2842 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Ala' al-Razi al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you intends a journey, let him bid farewell to his brothers, for they add to his supplication with their supplication goodness."" No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl except Yahya; Amr alone narrated it."
"2846","2843 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Nothing has erased Islam like miserliness has erased it."" No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Ali ibn Abi Sarah; Amr ibn al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"2847","2844 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Urwah, from A'ishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Do not declare any of the people of your qiblah a disbeliever for a sin, even if they commit major sins; and pray behind every imam, and strive with every commander."" No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Ali ibn Abi Sarah; Amr ibn al-Husayn alone narrated it."
"2848","2845 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Walid ibn Sa'dan narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh and Abu Wa'il, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud who said: It is as if I look at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving salam to his right: ""Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,"" and to his left: ""Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."""
"2849","2846 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' informed us, Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr ""{Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High},"" ""{Say: O disbelievers},"" and ""{Say: He is Allah, the One}."" No one narrated these hadiths from Asim except Abd al-Malik."
"2850","2847 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Matar narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating in Makkah, when Iblis came intending to step on his neck. So Jibril struck him a blow with his wing, and his feet did not settle on the ground until he reached Jordan. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Uthman ibn Matar."
"2851","2848 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Umm Umar bint Hassan ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Ghusn narrated to us, she said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Qays ibn Isa narrated to me, from his father, that Hafsah said: O Messenger of Allah, is it that when you fall ill you put Abu Bakr forward? He said: ""It is not I who put him forward, but Allah Who put him forward."" This hadith is not narrated from Yahya ibn Qays except with this chain; al-Salt alone narrated it."
"2852","2849 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to me, from his father, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and met him at al-Baqi'. I heard him saying: ""Peace be upon the inhabitants of the abodes among the believers."" My sandal strap broke, and he said to me: ""Fix your foot?"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, my estrangement has been long, and I am far from the abode of my people. He said: ""O Bashir, do you not praise Allah Who took your forelock to Islam from among Rabi'ah - a people who think that were it not for them, the earth would be overturned with those upon it."" No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except his son Ishaq; Uqbah alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Bashir except with this chain."
"2853","2850 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever ascends the pass - the pass of al-Murar - there shall be removed from him what was removed from the Children of Israel."" Jabir said: The first to ascend it were our horses of Banu al-Khazraj, then the people followed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All of you are forgiven except the owner of the red camel."" We said: Come, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) may seek forgiveness for you. He said: Finding my lost camel is dearer to me than that your companion seek forgiveness for me - and he was searching for a lost camel. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah ibn Khalid except Mu'adh."
"2854","2851 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Bilal is, and the mu'adhdhins are the longest-necked of people."" No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Husam ibn Misakk."
"2855","2852 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata', from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he eats of the voluntary sacrificial meat, he has incurred liability."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Khalid alone narrated it."
"2856","2853 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad who said: Abu Qu'ays narrated to me that he came to A'ishah and asked permission to enter upon her, and she disliked giving him permission. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, she said: O Prophet of Allah, Abu Qu'ays came to me and I refused to permit him. He said: ""Let your uncle enter upon you."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, only the woman nursed me; the man did not nurse me. He said: ""He is your uncle, so let him enter upon you."" And Abu Qu'ays was the brother of A'ishah's foster-mother. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qu'ays except with this chain; Hudbah alone narrated it."
"2857","2854 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to me, from Ubaydillah ibn Musa, from Abu Mada' - and he was a truthful man - from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Subayh, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from his grandfather Subayh who said: I was at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan and al-Husayn came and sat aside. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: ""You are upon good"" - and over him was a Khaybari cloak. He covered them with it and said: ""I am at war with whoever wars against you, at peace with whoever makes peace with you."" This hadith is not narrated from Subayh, the freedman of Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except with this chain; Husayn al-Ashqar alone narrated it. And al-Suddi narrated it from Subayh, from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"2858","2855 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Harb Abu Bishr al-Muzani narrated to us, al-Mada' al-Kharraz informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shake hands with women from beneath the garment. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Mada'; Attab alone narrated it."
"2859","2856 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad, the nephew of Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, narrated to us, he said: A shaykh surnamed Abu Muhammad narrated to me, and a shaykh called al-Muhajir narrated to me, in the time of Khalaf in the great mosque, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your Lord Almighty has breezes in the days of your time, so expose yourselves to them; perhaps one of you will be touched by a breeze from them after which he will never be wretched."" This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad ibn Maslamah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Abdah alone narrated it."
"2860","2857 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to me, he said: I heard Salamah ibn al-Akwa' raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say when the wind blew fiercely: ""O Allah, a fertilizing wind, not a barren one."" No one narrated this hadith from Yazid, the freedman of Salamah, except al-Mughirah; Ahmad ibn Abdah alone narrated it."
"2861","2858 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri who said: I said to Damrah ibn Abdillah ibn Unays: What did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to your father about Laylat al-Qadr? He said: My father was a desert-dweller. He said: O Messenger of Allah, command me a night in which I may come down. He said: ""Come down on the twenty-third night."" When he turned away, he said: ""Seek it in the last ten."" No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr except Fudayl."
"2862","2859 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever the sea casts up and recedes from, eat it; and whatever dies in it or floats, do not eat it."" No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il except Yahya."
"2863","2860 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Ash'ath ibn Sulaym, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The days of tashriq are days of eating and drinking, so let no one fast them."" No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Sharik, and no one from Sharik except Husayn ibn al-Ashqar; Ahmad ibn Abdah alone narrated it."
"2864","2861 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Jabir, from Abdillah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, and from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Abbas, from Ali who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to drink in a vessel of silver. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Qays."
"2865","2862 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Zadham, from Salman who said: I had a nosebleed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: ""Perform ablution."" No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far except Husayn al-Ashqar."
"2866","2863 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Bakhit al-Tahi, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me of three, which I shall never abandon in life: witr before sleep, fasting three days of every month, and the Duha prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Nuh."
"2867","2864 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Muslim al-Khashshab narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whatever is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire."" No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Sulaym."
"2868","2865 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Mujalid narrated to us, from his father, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq who said: I asked A'ishah about the voluntary prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while traveling? She said: ""Two rak'ahs after every prayer."" No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except his son."
"2869","2866 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Dinar, from Yazid al-Rishk who said: I heard Abu Zayd - and he had companionship - saying: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in one of the paths of Madinah, when he heard a man praying tahajjud and reciting the Mother of the Quran. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and listened until he completed it, then said: ""There is nothing in the Quran like it."" This hadith is not narrated from Abu Zayd Amr ibn Akhtab except with this chain; Sulaym ibn Muslim alone narrated it."
"2870","2867 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to the prayer ground walking, and return walking - and Abu Bakr and Umar too. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah ibn Umar except Abd al-Rahman."
"2871","2868 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja' al-Makki narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever avoids them is more innocent in his religion and honor, and whoever falls into doubtful matters will soon fall into the unlawful - like one who grazes around a sanctuary, soon to encroach upon the sanctuary without realizing."" No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Abdillah."
"2872","2869 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: When Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the Quran, the first thing he cast upon him was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. When Jibril said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, a second time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that the surah had been sealed."
"2873","2870 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from his father, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Ali to Fatimah, he said: O Ali, do not enter upon your wife until you present something to them. He said: I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: ""Give her your Hutamiyyah armor."" Ibn Abi Rawwad said: My father said: ""The armor was valued at four hundred and eighty dirhams."""
"2874","2871 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu Umar al-Ghudani, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""No man shall have camels for which he does not pay their due in their hardship and ease, except that on the Day of Resurrection a flat, smooth plain will be spread for them; they will come as their most numerous, fattest, most cheerful and largest, and trample him with their hooves. Whenever the last of them passes, the first returns - on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years."" And he said concerning sheep something similar, and concerning gold and silver something similar."
"2875","2872 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ja'd - or Ibn Abi al-Ja'd - from Abu Umamah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought the apportioned share of Banu so-and-so and gained such-and-such in it. He said: ""Shall I not inform you of what is more profitable than it?"" He said: Does it exist? He said: ""A man who learns ten verses."" So the man went and learned ten verses, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. No one narrated these hadiths from Sulayman al-Taymi except his son."
"2876","2873 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi al-Fadl, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that any odor be found from him that causes annoyance. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Imran; Isma'il alone narrated it."
"2877","2874 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, the brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am holding your waistbands, saying: Beware of the Fire and beware of the prescribed punishments - three times. Then I shall precede you at the Pool; whoever comes to it will succeed. Men will be brought until, when I recognize them and they recognize me, they will be snatched away from me. I shall say: My Lord, my companions. It will be said: They kept turning back on their heels."" No one narrated this hadith except Abd al-Wahid."
"2878","2875 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Hilal, the brother of Banu Murrah ibn Abbad, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: We suffered severe need, so my family ordered me to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for something. I came forward, and the first thing I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying was: ""Whoever seeks independence, Allah will make him independent; whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste; and whoever asks us, we shall not withhold anything from him if we find it."" I said to myself: I shall surely seek independence so Allah will make me independent, and I shall surely be chaste so Allah will make me chaste. So I did not ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anything."
"2879","2876 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""What is between the two sides of my Pool is as between Sana'a and Madinah."""
"2880","2877 - And with the same chain, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I repent to Allah in a day seventy times."""
"2881","2878 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: When we returned from the expedition of al-Hudaybiyyah, having been barred from our rites, in grief and sorrow, Allah Almighty revealed: ""{Indeed We have granted you a clear victory}"" to the end of the verse. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There has been revealed to me a verse better than the world and all it contains."" No one narrated these hadiths from Sulayman al-Taymi except his son."
"2882","2879 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu al-Jawza' who said: Ibn Abbas said to me: O Abu al-Jawza', shall I not inform you, shall I not give you a gift, shall I not give you? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Whoever prays four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah the Mother of the Quran and a surah, then when he finishes the recitation says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest - this is one - until he completes fifteen, then bows and says it ten times, then rises and says it ten times, then prostrates and says it ten times, then rises and says it ten times, then prostrates and says it ten times, then raises his head and says it ten times - these are seventy-five in each rak'ah - until he finishes four rak'ahs."" He said: ""Whoever prays them, all his sins will be forgiven - small and great, old or recent, past or to come."" No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Yahya ibn Uqbah; Muhriz alone narrated it."
"2883","2880 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn Zunbur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, and Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to al-Safa from the gate of Banu Makhzum. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Abd al-Rahman."
"2884","2881 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Part of the excellence of a man's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him."" No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah."
"2885","2882 - Ibrahim narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr informed us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."""
"2886","2883 - And with the same chain, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third valley, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents."""
"2887","2884 - And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Between his eyes is written: Disbeliever"" - meaning the Dajjal."
"2888","2885 - And with the same chain, from Anas who said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken up to Paradise, a river was shown to him whose banks were hollow pearls. The angel with him struck with his hand and brought out musk. He said to the angel with him: What is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah Almighty gave you. He said: Then Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for me, and I saw a great light at it."
"2889","2886 - And with the same chain, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""When the disbeliever does a good deed, he is fed a morsel for it in this world; as for the believer, Allah Almighty stores his good deeds for him in the Hereafter, and grants him provision in this world in return for his obedience."""
"2890","2887 - And with the same chain, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: ""When the people of Paradise see them, they will say: Who are these? It will be said: These are the Jahannamiyyun."""
"2891","2888 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from his father who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reciting: ""{Rivalry has distracted you}."" He said: ""The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. And what do you have of your wealth, O son of Adam, except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave and sent forth."""
"2892","2889 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""When Allah decreed creation, He wrote in a book with Him: My mercy has overcome - or he said: has preceded - My anger."""
"2893","2890 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abdillah, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Woman is nakedness, and when she goes out, Satan looks toward her. She is never closer to Allah than when she is in the depths of her house."""
"2894","2891 - And with the same chain, from Qatadah, from Khulayd ibn Abdillah al-Asari, from Abu al-Darda', from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""No sun rises or sets except that at its two sides are two angels calling, heard by all on earth except the two heavy ones: O people, hasten to your Lord; what is little and suffices is better than what is abundant and distracts. And it never returns except that at its two sides are two angels calling: O Allah, whoever spends, give him a successor; and whoever withholds, give him destruction."""
"2895","2892 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Husayn ibn Abdillah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating at Arafah, with his hands to his chest like the begging of the poor. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid."
"2896","2893 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Umar ibn Rashid al-Yamami, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his father, from his grandfather, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be leaders who do not follow my guidance nor adopt my practice, and there will be men whose hearts are the hearts of devils in the bodies of men."" I said: What should I do if I live to see that? He said: ""You listen and obey the supreme commander, even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth; listen and obey."" No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Umar; Ibn Sallam alone narrated it."
"2897","2894 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Taifi narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Isma'il ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Men will govern your affairs after me who will make you recognize what you disapprove, and disapprove toward you what you recognize. So there is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah."""
"2898","2895 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Sayhan narrated to us, he said: Halbas ibn Muhammad al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married off my daughter and I would like you to help me with something. He said: ""I have nothing, but when tomorrow comes, come to me bringing a wide-headed bottle and a tree stick. And a sign between me and you is that I close the side of the door."" He said: So he brought him a wide-headed bottle and a tree stick. He began scraping the sweat from his forearms until the bottle filled. He said: ""Take it, and order your daughter, when she wants to perfume herself, to dip this stick in the bottle and perfume herself with it."" He said: When she perfumed herself, the people of Madinah would smell the fragrance of that perfume, so they were called the house of the perfumed. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Sufyan, and no one from Sufyan except Halbas; Bishr alone narrated it."
"2899","2896 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: al-Dhayyal ibn Ubayd ibn Hanzalah narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather Hanzalah ibn Hidhaym saying: I came as a delegate with my grandfather Hidhaym to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sons with beards and others, and this is the youngest of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought me near and wiped my head, and said: ""May Allah bless you."" Al-Dhayyal said: I saw Hanzalah being brought a man with a swollen face and a sheep with a swollen udder. He would say: In the name of Allah, upon the spot of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and wipe it, and the swelling would go away. This hadith is not narrated from Hanzalah except with this chain; Abu Sa'id alone narrated it."
"2900","2897 - Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Aws, from Bilal ibn Yahya who said: I heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Ammar is such-and-such and such-and-such, so long as old age has not reached him."" This hadith is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain; Sa'd ibn Aws al-Katib alone narrated it."
"2901","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to give two salutations (taslims) in the prayer."
"2902","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Yuhmadi narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two men love one another for the sake of Allah except that the more beloved of them to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is the one with stronger love for his companion. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr."
"2903","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to me, from Salim Abu Abdullah ibn Salim, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Fast from one new moon crescent to the next new moon crescent. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Malih except Salim, nor from Salim except al-Mufaddal; Abu Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"2904","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Musa narrated to us, he said: Salm narrated to us, from Umar ibn Nabhan, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing sandals and leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar; Salm is alone in transmitting it."
"2905","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: Uwayn ibn Amr al-Qaysi, brother of Riyah ibn Amr, narrated to us, he said: Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Recite the Quran with sorrow, for it was sent down with sorrow."
"2906","And with the same chain from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: In Paradise there are chambers whose outside can be seen from their inside and whose inside can be seen from their outside; Allah has prepared them for those who love one another for His sake, visit one another for His sake, and give to one another for His sake. No one narrated these two hadiths from Said except Uwayn; Ismail is alone in transmitting them."
"2907","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: Jafar al-Dubai narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals, and sometimes he took them off. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar except Ismail."
"2908","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Suqayr narrated to us, he said: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to me, he said: I saw Anas ibn Malik at al-Zawiyah, and I said: Tell me about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how was it? For it has reached me that you used to perform ablution for him. He said: Yes. Then he called for water for ablution, and a basin and a carved cup were brought, carved as it was in its ground, and placed before him. He poured water over his hands, washed his palms thoroughly, then rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, then brought out his right hand and washed it three times, then washed the left three times, then wiped his head once, except that he passed it over his ears and wiped them, then he put both his palms together into the water, then he mentioned the hadith."
"2909","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Zilal narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Two men crossed a desert: a worshipper, and another afflicted with frivolity/recklessness. The worshipper became thirsty until he fell, and his companion kept looking at him, having with him a small water vessel with some water in it. He kept looking at him while he lay fallen, and said: By Allah, if this righteous servant dies of thirst while I have water, I will never attain any good from Allah; but if I give him my water to drink, I will die. So he relied upon Allah and resolved, sprinkled some of his water upon him and gave him the remainder to drink, and he stood up until they both crossed the desert. Then the one afflicted with recklessness will be stopped on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and ordered to the Fire; the angels will drive him, and he will see the worshipper and say: O so-and-so, do you know me? He will say: Who are you? He will say: I am so-and-so who preferred you over myself on the day of the desert. He will say: Yes, I know you. Then he will say to the angels: Stop, and they will stop, and he will come until he stands, then supplicate his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, saying: O Lord, You know his favor to me and how he preferred me over himself; O Lord, grant him to me. And He will say to him: He is yours. Then he will come and take his brother by the hand and admit him to Paradise. Jafar ibn Sulayman said: I said to Abu Zilal: Did Anas narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Zilal except Jafar; al-Salt is alone in transmitting it."
"2910","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Unays ibn Abi Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Salim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Gather your companions. So I went seeking them in the mosque one by one, waking them, and we came to the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered. A large dish of prepared food was placed before us, about two mudds of barley, and he said to us: Eat in the name of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when the dish was placed: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is nothing in the household of Muhammad except what you see. So we ate until we were full, and some remained, and we were between seventy and eighty. It was said to Abu Hurayrah: What was it like when you finished? He said: Like it was when it was placed, except that there were traces of fingers in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Salim except Unays ibn Abi Yahya."
"2911","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, with Aishah and Hafsah present, Ali entered, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he raised his head and said: Come near me, come near me. So he leaned him against himself, and he remained with him until he passed away. When he had passed, Ali stood up and closed the door, and al-Abbas came with the sons of Abd al-Muttalib and stood at the door. Ali kept saying: You remained pure in life and pure in death, and a pure fragrance diffused the like of which they had never found. He said: It is the fragrance of your moaning like the moaning of a woman; turn to your companion. Then Ali said: Admit al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas to me. The Ansar said: We adjure you by Allah regarding our share of the Messenger of Allah, so they admitted a man among them called Aws ibn Khawli, carrying a jar in one of his hands. They heard a voice in the house: Do not strip the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wash him as he is in his shirt. So Ali washed him, inserting his hand under the shirt, while al-Fadl held the garment away from him and the Ansari carried the water, with a cloth on Ali's hand as he inserted his hand under the shirt."
"2912","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Arabs used to make one year one month and one year two months, and they would only coincide with the Hajj once every twenty-six years, and that is the postponement (al-nasi) which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, mentioned in His Book. When in the year Abu Bakr performed Hajj with the people it coincided that year with the Hajj, so Allah called it the Greater Hajj. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj the following year, and the people faced the crescents anew, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time has turned back to its original state on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Dawud ibn Abi Hind, nor from Dawud except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Salt is alone in transmitting it."
"2913","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated while in Makkah at (Surat) al-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn and mankind prostrated with him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Warith."
"2914","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and the prayer comes, begin with supper. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Warith."
"2915","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn al-Jad al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing fresh ripe dates and unripe dates together. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn al-Jad except Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj."
"2916","Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Suqayr al-Araj narrated to us, he said: my father Suqayr narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day from his house with some of his Companions, took one of the roads of Madinah, and passed by the courtyard of a people where a dead kid goat lay thrown in their courtyard. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over it looking at it, then turned to his Companions and said: Do you see this kid, how worthless it is to its owners that they threw it away? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By Allah, this world is more insignificant to Allah than this kid is to its owners when they threw it away like this. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Bakkar ibn Suqayr is alone in transmitting it."
"2917","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Yasar Abu Rawh al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn Abi Maryam al-Saluli narrated to us, from his father, that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, forgive those who shave. A man among the people said: O Prophet of Allah, and those who shorten? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. The man said: O Prophet of Allah, and those who shorten? Until the fourth time he said: And those who shorten. No one narrated this hadith from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam except Hibban ibn Yasar."
"2918","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Najih Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but I am unable to do it. He said: Is any of your parents still alive? He said: My mother. He said: Present to Allah an excuse through dutifulness to her, for if you do that you are a pilgrim, a performer of umrah, and a mujahid; when your mother is pleased with you, so fear Allah and be dutiful to her. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Maymun."
"2919","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he was eating the heart of a palm tree with the people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among trees there is a tree like the Muslim man. The people fell silent until I almost asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), though I was the youngest of the people, then he said: It is the palm tree. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah except Yahya."
"2920","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ata, he said: al-Bahzi narrated to me, he said: I asked al-Husayn ibn Ali about the tashahhud of Ali, and he said: It is the tashahhud of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: Narrate to me the tashahhud of Ali from the tashahhud of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers, and good words, and morning and evening devotions, and pure, blissful, ample, clean devotions belong to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Ata except Amr."
"2921","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Abd al-Aziz."
"2922","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by children and greeted them."
"2923","And with the same chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out both, meaning Hajj and Umrah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Said except Muhammad ibn Sawa."
"2924","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, ten are written for him; whoever says it ten times, one hundred are written for him; whoever seeks Allah's forgiveness, He forgives him; whoever assists in a dispute unjustly or without knowledge remains under Allah's anger until he desists; whoever intercedes to block one of Allah's prescribed punishments has opposed Allah; and whoever dies owing a dinar or a dirham, it will be taken from his good deeds, for there there is neither dinar nor dirham. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"2925","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I was with my father at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: There will be for this ummah twelve custodians (rulers), those who abandon them will not harm them. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whispered a word I did not hear, so I said to my father: What was the word the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whispered? He said: All of them are from Quraysh. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said."
"2926","And with the same chain from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its right will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, though its fragrance is found from a distance of five hundred years. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Muhammad."
"2927","Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us, at Kufa in the year 288, he said: al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-Khazin narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between the east and the west is qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abu Mashar."
"2928","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-Khazin narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the husband of Barirah was a slave. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except Abu Hafs; al-Harith is alone in transmitting it."
"2929","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Marrar ibn Hammuyah al-Hamadhani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said Abu Zakariyya al-Madani, keeper of the grave of the Messenger of Allah, narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Qays, freedman of Banu al-Harith ibn Fihr, narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father Aslam who said: Umar performed Hajj in the year of al-Ramadah, year sixteen, until when he was between al-Suqya and al-Arj in the middle of the night, a rider on the road presented himself and shouted: O caravan, is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among you? Umar said to him: Woe to you, are you sane? He said: Sanity drove me to you. Has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away? They said: He has passed away, so he wept and the people wept. He said: Who took charge after him? They said: Ibn Abi Quhafah. He said: The most forbearing of Banu Taym? They said: Yes. He said: Is he among you? They said: He has passed away. Then he supplicated and the people supplicated, and he said: Who took charge after him? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. He said: The ruddy one of Banu Adi? They said: Yes, he is the one who spoke to you. He said: Where were you regarding the fair one of Banu Umayyah or the bald one of Banu Hashim? They said: That has passed; what is your need? He said: I met the Messenger of Allah when I was Abu Aqil al-Juayli, at the hollow of Juayl, and I embraced Islam and pledged allegiance, and I drank with him a drink of sawiq; he drank the first of it and gave me the last of it to drink. By Allah, I have continued to find its satiation whenever I hunger, its coolness whenever I thirst, and its quenching whenever I am parched, until this day of mine. Then I settled on this white mountain, I and my wife and daughters, and I would pray there five prayers every day and night, fast a month in the year, and sacrifice on the tenth of Dhu al-Hijjah; that is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me. Until this year entered, and by Allah, no sheep remained for us except one sheep which the wolf attacked last night, eating part of it while we ate part, so help, help. Umar said: Help has come to you; join us at the water in the morning. Umar went on until he reached the water, kept waiting, and delayed departure for his sake, but he did not come. So he called the keeper of the water and said: Abu Aqil al-Juayli has three daughters and his wife with him; when he comes to you, spend upon him, his family and his children until I pass by you on my return, if Allah wills. When Umar finished his Hajj he returned and called the keeper of the water, saying: What became of Abu Aqil? He said: He came to me the next day after you spoke to me, feverish; he was ill with me for nights, then died; that is his grave. Umar turned to his companions and said: Allah was not pleased for him to be tried through you. Then he stood among the people, prayed over him, and took charge of his daughters and wife, spending upon them. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Aqil except with this chain; Marrar is alone in transmitting it."
"2930","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abdullah al-Khazin narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to brush his mouth with the siwak."
"2931","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Marrar ibn Hammuyah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Jarwal ibn Janfal al-Harrani narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for one of his wives with a pot of harisah."
"2932","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Isam al-Jurjani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: Umar addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us in my standing place among you and said: Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then lying will spread until a man testifies though not asked to testify, and a man swears though not asked to swear. Whoever wants the heart of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the one alone and is farther from two. Verily, let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Verily, whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Shubah except Abu Dawud; Abd al-Hamid is alone in transmitting it."
"2933","Ibrahim ibn Nailah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Ubaydah al-Tammar narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Saj, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Sad ibn Ubaydah and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hind, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: A man of the Haruriyyah came and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I wish you had died with your companions and not remained after them; you turned to Hajj and Umrah and abandoned jihad? He answered the Haruri: May your mother be bereaved of you; if I were to remain after them fifty years weeping, I would have been created for regret. Then Abdullah ibn Umar said: Islam is built upon five: that Allah be worshipped, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House of Allah, and fasting Ramadan. A man of the notables of Syria sitting with him said: That you worship Allah, do you command it? He said: Yes. He said: Then he counted fasting before Hajj? He said: I do not make it except the last of them; thus I heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2934","And with the same chain from Uthman ibn Saj, from Khusayf, from Mujahid and Ikrimah and Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he mentioned wiping over the leather socks in the presence of Umar: Sad and Abdullah ibn Umar mentioned it, and Umar said: Sad is more knowledgeable than you. Abdullah ibn Abbas said: O Sad, we do not deny that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped, but did he wipe after Surat al-Maidah was revealed? No one spoke, for it made everything precise, and it was the last surah revealed of the Quran except Baraah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Mutamir except Ubayd."
"2935","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Aradah al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali narrated to us, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise. Abu al-Darda said: Even if he commits adultery and steals? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if he commits adultery and steals, despite Abu al-Darda. No one narrated it from Raja except Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, nor narrated it from Muhammad except Abdullah ibn Aradah."
"2936","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and said in his sermon: My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to teach you what you are ignorant of from what He taught me on this day of mine: All wealth I grant My servant is lawful, and I created My servants all as upright (hunafa); then the devils came to them and diverted them from their religion, forbade them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, looked at the people of the earth and abhorred them, their non-Arabs and their Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book, and said: I sent you only to test you and to test others through you; I sent down upon you a Book which water does not wash away, you recite it sleeping and awake. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to confront Quraysh, so I said: O Lord, then they will split my head and leave it like a loaf of bread. He said: Expel them as they expelled you, fight them and We will support you, spend and We will spend upon you, send an army and We will send five like it of angels. No one narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Abd al-Wahhab, nor narrated it from Abd al-Wahhab except al-Muqaddami."
"2937","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness. No one narrated it from Qatadah except Said, nor from Said except Abu Ubaydah, nor from Abu Ubaydah except Said al-Jarmi."
"2938","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr al-Muzalliq narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has servants who recognize people by discernment (tawassum). No one narrated it from Thabit except Abu Bishr, nor from Abu Bishr except Abu Ubaydah."
"2939","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Rumayh ibn Hilal al-Tai, he said: Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father who said: We prayed Zuhr behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he finished his prayer he turned to us angry and called out in a voice that made the virgins in their chambers hear, saying: O company of those who embraced Islam but faith has not entered their hearts, do not harm the Muslims and do not seek their faults, for whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will expose his cover and reveal his fault even if inside his house. It is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain."
"2940","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pulpits of gold will be placed for the prophets and they will sit upon them, while my pulpit remains and I will not sit upon it, standing before my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, upright, out of concern for my ummah, fearing He will send me to Paradise while my ummah remains after me. So I will say: O Lord, my ummah, my ummah. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: O Muhammad, what do you want Me to do with your ummah? I will say: O Lord, settle their reckoning swiftly. They will be called and reckoned; among them are those who enter Paradise by Allah's mercy, and among them those who enter Paradise by my intercession. I will continue to intercede until I am given documents for men already sent to the Fire, until Malik, keeper of the Fire, says: O Muhammad, you have left nothing of your Lord's anger against your ummah as retribution. No one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Thabit except Abu Ubaydah."
"2941","Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah who said: Aishah said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel for major impurity, and I would say: Leave some for me, leave some for me. We do not know of Abu Umamah narrating from Aishah anything besides this, and it is not narrated except by this route."
"2942","Ibrahim ibn Sharik al-Asadi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Ikrimah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man being killed defending his wealth is martyrdom. Thus Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated it from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Ikrimah, from Abdullah ibn Amr. And Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan but differed from Suayr in his narration:"
"2943","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Hasan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Isa ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and fights and is killed is a martyr. And from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan there is another chain: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his wealth sought unjustly and fights for it and is killed is a martyr. And the hadith has been narrated from Ikrimah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, without the narration of Abdullah ibn al-Hasan: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fights for his wealth until killed wrongfully is a martyr."
"2944","Ibrahim ibn Sharik narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Thawr, from Mamar, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves noble matters and dislikes trivial ones."
"2945","Ibrahim ibn Mattuyah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasabi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ayyub, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed would raise his hands when beginning the prayer, when saying takbir for bowing, and when raising his head from bowing. No one narrated it from Ayyub except Ibn Dhi Himayah."
"2946","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Araj, and another man, both testifying about Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of Fajr prayer before the sun rises has not missed it, and whoever catches a rakah of Asr prayer before the sun sets has not missed it. No one narrated it from Rawh except Muhammad, nor from Muhammad except Abdullah."
"2947","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, from Shubah, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that Umar said: Friday is two rakahs, Fitr is two rakahs, Adha is two rakahs, and travel is two rakahs, complete without shortening, upon the tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated it from Shubah except Sufyan."
"2948","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Rahmah al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids a wrongdoer with falsehood to refute a truth with his falsehood has disavowed the protection of Allah and His Messenger; whoever eats a dirham of usury is like thirty-three adulteries; and whose flesh grows from ill-gotten gains, the Fire is more deserving of him. No one narrated it from Ibrahim except Muhammad, nor narrated it from Muhammad ibn Himyar except Said."
"2949","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah who said: The mother of the sons of Abu Talhah came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth; is ghusl obligatory upon a woman if she sees what a man sees? I laughed and said: Does a woman have a wet dream? He said: Yes; otherwise how would the child resemble its mother? No one narrated it from Rawh except Ibn Ulayyah."
"2950","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Bazzaz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged regarding the fetus with a ghurrah: a slave, or a slave-girl, or a horse, or a mule. A group narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr, but none of them said: or a horse, or a mule, except Isa ibn Yunus."
"2951","Ibrahim ibn Bundar al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Misar, from Musa ibn Abi Kathir, from Mujahid, from Aishah who said: I was eating hays with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a large cup when Umar passed; he invited him and he ate, and his finger touched my finger, so he said: How sensitive; oh, oh; if I were obeyed concerning you, no eye would see you. Then the verse of hijab was revealed. No one narrated it from Misar except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"2952","Ibrahim ibn Asbat ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Malik al-Khuwarizmi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: We did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more often than we fasted thirty. No one narrated it from Hammad except Abd al-Ala."
"2953","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Masruq, that he said to Ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt: Abdullah ibn Masud narrated to us, and he was not a liar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that your father's neck be struck while captive and he did not ransom him. He said: Who will care for the children after me? He said: For them is the Fire; sufficient for you is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approved for you. No one narrated it from Amr ibn Murrah except Zayd."
"2954","Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Marwan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the hypocrite: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when you trust him he betrays you. No one narrated it from Zayd except his son Abd al-Rahman, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except by this route."
"2955","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Zahmawayh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Jabir ibn al-Hurr and Amr Abu Muharrar and Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah and Kathir al-Nawwa and Abd al-Malik ibn Sulayman, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see the star in the sky, and Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent. No one narrated it from Ali ibn Hashim except Zahmawayh."
"2956","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Samaah narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Fatimah bint Qays, that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said that she suffered prolonged bleeding; he reportedly said: That is a vein; when it comes, leave prayer, and when it ends, bathe and wash the blood from yourself, then pray. No one narrated it from al-Awzai except Ibn Samaah, nor narrated it from him except Imran; and Fatimah bint Qays here is Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh."
"2957","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Madan narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits - or two qualities - are easy, yet few act upon them: the five prayers; you glorify Allah after each prayer ten times, praise Him ten times, and magnify Him ten times, making one hundred fifty on the tongue and one thousand five hundred in the balance; and when you go to your bed you glorify, magnify and praise one hundred times, making one hundred on the tongue and one thousand in the balance. No one narrated it from Misar except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah, and Abu Usamah."
"2958","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Ghazzal al-Misri al-Muaddal narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek Allah's forgiveness every day and repent to Him one hundred times."
"2959","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn al-Asbagh narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, this greeting of peace upon you we know, but how about sending blessings? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious; O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. No one narrated it from Salamah except Misar, nor narrated it from Misar except Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, nor narrated it from Abu Bakr except Maymun."
"2960","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Amr al-Hadhda al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Dahhak, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten the prayer at al-Aqiq. It is not narrated from Ibn Umar in raised (marfu) form except by this route."
"2961","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Irq al-Yahsabi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hafs al-Awsabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Umm al-Darda who said: I asked Aishah: What would you provision the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with when you traveled with him, or performed Hajj or went on expedition with him? She said: I would provision him with a bottle of oil, a comb, a mirror, scissors, a kohl container, and a siwak. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Hafs is alone in transmitting it."
"2962","Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Tawwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Yahya al-Daybuli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Yahya al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, from Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says at his death: There is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Fire will never touch him."
"2963","He said: And Jabir ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. And I heard him say: Do not abandon the two rakahs before Fajr prayer, for therein are precious rewards. And I heard him say: Do not die with a debt upon you, for there are only good deeds and bad deeds; there is neither dinar nor dirham there; recompense and retribution; Allah wrongs no one."
"2964","Ibrahim ibn Ayyub al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Fatimah bint Qays said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the woman with prolonged bleeding. He said: She counts the days of her menstrual periods, then bathes at each time of purity, then stuffs (a cloth), and prays. No one narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Jafar."
"2965","Ibrahim ibn Darastawayh al-Fasawi narrated to us, he said: Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his circumambulation at al-Marwah."
"2966","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Hajari al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-Abbas came visiting the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his illness, lifted him and seated him in his place on the bed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah raise you, O uncle. Al-Abbas said: This is Ali seeking permission. He said: Let him enter. So he entered with al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Al-Abbas said: These are your sons, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And they are your sons, O uncle. He said: Do you love them? He said: May Allah love you as I love them."
"2967","Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha Muslim ibn Subayh, from Ibn Abbas who said: al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, we recognize hatred in the faces of some people. He said: How do you recognize it? He said: There is a circle talking, and when you appear to them they fall silent due to my kinship to you; had they been sincere to Allah and His Messenger they would not fall silent due to my kinship to you. He said: Do you know them? He said: Yes. Al-Abbas placed his hand on the arm of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then entered the mosque, and al-Abbas said to him: This circle is among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took al-Abbas by the hand and raised it, saying: Whoever does not love this uncle of mine for Allah and for his kinship to me is not a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ibn al-Ajlah."
"2968","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq ibn al-Asamm al-Akkawi narrated to us at Akka, he said: Munakhkhal ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Umar ibn Subh, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fights in the sea in the path of Allah - and Allah knows best who fights in His path - has fulfilled all obedience to Allah, sought Paradise by every seeking, and fled the Fire by every fleeing. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Umar; Muhammad ibn Himyar is alone in transmitting it."
"2969","Ibrahim ibn Bayan al-Jawhari al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jufi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from Misar, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man wakes his wife at night and they perform ablution and pray, they are written among the men and women who remember Allah much. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Jafar; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"2970","Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbade you from visiting graves; now visit them, but do not speak obscene/indecent speech; I forbade you vessels, so drink in whatever you wish but do not become intoxicated; and I forbade you the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, so keep whatever you wish. No one narrated it from Simak except Muhammad."
"2971","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, he said: Musa al-Qari informed us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no prophet nor ruler except that he has two confidants: a confidant who commands him to good and forbids him evil, and a confidant who spares him no corruption; whoever is protected from its evil has been protected. No one narrated it from al-Awzai except al-Mufaddal, nor narrated it from al-Mufaddal except Musa; it is the hadith of Ishaq."
"2972","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas who said: On the morning I had a wet dream, I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him I had a wet dream. He said: Do not enter upon women. No day was harder upon me than it. No one narrated it from Yahya except Malik, nor from Malik except Zafir."
"2973","Ismail ibn Qirat al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shaving the back of the neck except for cupping."
"2974","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends two pairs of his wealth in the path of Allah, the keepers of Paradise will call him on the Day of Resurrection, each inviting him to what it has: O so-and-so, this is good."
"2975","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ata, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call this Stone to witness goodness, for on the Day of Resurrection it will be an accepted intercessor, with a tongue and two lips, testifying for whoever touched it. No one narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha except al-Walid."
"2976","Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Sulayman, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The children of the polytheists are servants of the people of Paradise. No one narrated it from Qatadah except Muqatil."
"2977","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn al-Muhajir al-Qurashi al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights his companion, let him avoid the face."
"2978","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Amir al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade, in the expedition of Awtas, that a man have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth. No one narrated it from Dawud except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except Ismail."
"2979","Ismail ibn Abdullah al-Dabbi al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Hammad ibn al-Furafisah al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: al-Khalil ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early mornings. We heard it only from this shaykh, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except by this route."
"2980","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Muhammad ibn Shawdhab narrated to us, from Isa al-Azraq, from Matar al-Warraq, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he put his hand under his chin and ran his fingers through his beard. I said: What is this? He said: Thus my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me. It is not narrated from Matar except with this chain."
"2981","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, that he asked her about the vessels the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade. She said: He forbade gourds, green glazed jars, hollowed stumps, and pitched vessels. I said: What are these green jars; are they the hantam? She said: No; they are red jars in which pitch was carried, and wine was carried in them from Egypt to Madinah, so he forbade them. No one narrated it from Abu Hamzah except Yazid."
"2982","Ismail narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except Musa; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it."
"2983","Ismail ibn Numayl al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Hayyan, from Abu Hayyaj al-Asadi, from Ali ibn Rabiah al-Walibi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Fajr prayer on Friday, in the first rakah Alif Lam Mim, the revelation of al-Sajdah, and in the second rakah: Has there come upon man."
"2984","Ismail ibn Muhammad Abu Qusay al-Udhri al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Yazid al-Faqir, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to bathe on Friday."
"2985","Ismail ibn Ahmad al-Basri, agent of Aktham, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Suayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was only sent as a gifted mercy."
"2986","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud who said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How can I know when I do good and when I do bad? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear your neighbors say: You have done good, then you have done good; and when you hear them say: You have done bad, then you have done bad. No one narrated it from Mansur except Mamar, and it is not narrated from Ibn Masud except by this route."
"2987","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated would spread his arms until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen. No one narrated it from Mansur except Mamar, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"2988","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Awf, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he disliked - or forbade - sleeping before it and talking after it. No one narrated it from al-Thawri except Abd al-Razzaq."
"2989","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straightening the row is part of the perfection of prayer. No one narrated it from Ibn Aqil except Mamar, and it is not narrated from Jabir except by this route."
"2990","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abu Masud al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of what people learned from the first prophethood: if you have no shame, do whatever you wish. No one narrated it from al-Amash except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Abd al-Razzaq."
"2991","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Salman al-Farisi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will enter Paradise except with a pass: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is a book from Allah to so-and-so son of so-and-so: admit him to a lofty Paradise whose clusters hang near."
"2992","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a right over Quraysh, and Quraysh have a right over you: as long as they judge justly, fulfill trusts when entrusted, and show mercy when asked for mercy; whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhib except Mamar; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in transmitting it."
"2993","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner confidants to whom I retreated; so accept from their doers of good and overlook their doers of bad, for they have fulfilled what was upon them and what remains is what is for them. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Mamar."
"2994","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he saw rain would say: O Allah, a wholesome, pleasant rain. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
"2995","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant gives charity from wholesome earnings, Allah accepts it from him, takes it with His right hand, and nurtures it as one of you nurtures his foal or young camel; a man gives a date in charity and it grows in Allah's hand - or he said: in Allah's palm - until it becomes like a mountain, so give charity. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
"2996","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Urwah ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The giving hand is better than the lower hand. No one narrated this hadith from Simak ibn al-Fadl except Mamar; and the grandfather of Urwah ibn Muhammad is Atiyyah al-Sadi."
"2997","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah who said: A man said: What is sin, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Sin is what pricks your chest, so leave it. He said: What is faith? He said: Whoever is grieved by his bad deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Mamar, and it is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain."
"2998","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Ashath ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while people were with him, and a man among those with him said: I love this man for Allah's sake. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you told him? He said: No. He said: Go to him and tell him. So he went to him and told him, and he said: May the One for whom you loved me love you. Then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he asked him, and he told him what he said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are with whom you love, and you have what you intended. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath ibn Abdullah except Mamar."
"2999","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard people disputing, so he said: Those before you perished only through this: they struck parts of Allah's Book against others; Allah's Book was only revealed with parts confirming others, so do not deny parts of it through others. What you know of it, say it; what you do not know, entrust it to one who knows it. No one narrated this hadith except Mamar."
"3000","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: A Makhzumi woman used to borrow goods and deny them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her hand to be cut off. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar."
